window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":8,"qs":[{"id":"E1A-67","d":1,"ts":"1.1.11","t":"EventBridge archive and replay","q":"A company publishes business events to a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus. A new analytics consumer will be added next month, and it must process all events that were published during the previous 30 days, in addition to new events. Which solution meets this requirement with the LEAST custom development?","o":["Increase the EventBridge rule retry policy to 30 days.","Enable CloudTrail data events and reconstruct the events from the logs.","Create a Lambda function that writes every event to an Amazon DynamoDB table and later scans the table to resend events.","Create an EventBridge archive on the event bus with a retention period of at least 30 days, and start a replay to the new consumer's rule when it is deployed."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: konsumen baru harus memproses 'all events that were published during the previous 30 days' dengan 'LEAST custom development'. EventBridge archive menyimpan event dari sebuah event bus (dengan pola filter opsional) selama periode retensi tertentu, dan fitur replay mengirim ulang event yang diarsipkan dalam rentang waktu tertentu ke bus, sehingga rule konsumen baru menerimanya. Distraktor terdekat adalah menyimpan event ke DynamoDB dengan Lambda lalu mengirim ulang: berfungsi, tetapi semuanya kode kustom. CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan isi event bisnis kustom. Retry policy rule hanya berlaku untuk pengiriman yang gagal ke target yang sudah ada dan maksimum 24 jam. Aturan umum: replay event EventBridge = archive + replay.","r":["Salah — Retry policy hanya untuk kegagalan pengiriman (maksimum 24 jam), bukan replay historis.","Salah — CloudTrail tidak menyimpan isi event bisnis kustom yang dipublikasikan ke bus.","Salah — Membutuhkan kode kustom untuk menyimpan dan mengirim ulang event.","Benar — Archive menyimpan event selama periode retensi dan replay mengirimkannya kembali untuk konsumen baru."],"k":"Replay event EventBridge → archive + replay."},{"id":"E1A-19","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"AWS Glue job bookmarks","q":"An AWS Glue job runs every night and reads an Amazon RDS for MySQL table through a JDBC connection. The table has an auto-incrementing order_id column, and rows are never updated after insertion. Currently the job reads the entire table every night. The data engineer wants each run to read only the rows added since the previous successful run, with the LEAST development effort. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler on the RDS table before every job run.","Store the last processed order_id in an Amazon DynamoDB table and add custom code to query only newer rows.","Replace the Glue job with an AWS DMS task that performs a full load every night.","Enable AWS Glue job bookmarks and specify order_id as the bookmark key."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'auto-incrementing order_id', 'rows are never updated', dan 'LEAST development effort'. AWS Glue job bookmarks menyimpan state run sebelumnya; untuk sumber JDBC, bookmark memakai kolom kunci yang naik monoton (jobBookmarkKeys) sehingga run berikutnya hanya membaca baris dengan nilai lebih besar. Karena baris tidak pernah di-update, kolom auto-increment cukup untuk menangkap semua data baru. Distraktor terdekat adalah menyimpan watermark sendiri di DynamoDB: hasilnya sama tetapi butuh kode kustom yang harus dipelihara. DMS full load tetap membaca seluruh tabel. Crawler hanya memperbarui skema. Aturan umum: incremental load dari S3 atau JDBC di Glue = job bookmarks (JDBC: kunci monoton naik).","r":["Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, tidak membatasi baris yang dibaca.","Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi memerlukan kode kustom untuk menyimpan dan membaca watermark.","Salah — Full load tetap membaca seluruh tabel setiap malam.","Benar — Job bookmarks dengan order_id sebagai bookmark key membaca hanya baris baru tanpa kode tambahan."],"k":"Glue incremental dari JDBC → job bookmarks + kolom kunci monoton naik."},{"id":"E1A-09","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"DynamoDB Streams vs Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB","q":"A gaming company writes player state to an Amazon DynamoDB table. Five different teams want to consume the item-level changes for different purposes, and one team needs to reprocess up to 3 days of changes after deployments. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST custom development?","o":["Enable DynamoDB Streams and have all five teams read from the stream with AWS Lambda.","Enable Amazon Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB, set the data stream retention period to 7 days, and let each team consume the data stream.","Schedule DynamoDB exports to Amazon S3 every 3 days and share the exports with all teams.","Use AWS DMS with DynamoDB as the source and Amazon S3 as the target for change data capture."],"a":[1],"e":"Dua kata kunci yang menentukan: 'five different teams' (banyak consumer) dan 'reprocess up to 3 days'. DynamoDB Streams memiliki retensi tetap 24 jam dan disarankan tidak lebih dari dua proses membaca shard yang sama secara bersamaan, sehingga tidak memenuhi kedua syarat. Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB mengalirkan perubahan item ke sebuah Kinesis data stream yang retensinya bisa diperpanjang (hingga 365 hari) dan mendukung banyak consumer, termasuk enhanced fan-out. Export ke S3 tiap 3 hari bukan aliran perubahan. DMS tidak mendukung DynamoDB sebagai sumber CDC. Aturan umum: perubahan DynamoDB untuk banyak consumer atau retensi lebih dari 24 jam = Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB.","r":["Salah — DynamoDB Streams retensinya hanya 24 jam dan dibatasi sekitar dua reader bersamaan per shard.","Benar — Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB mendukung banyak consumer dan retensi yang dapat diperpanjang untuk replay.","Salah — Export berkala bukan aliran perubahan item dan tidak memenuhi kebutuhan konsumsi per perubahan.","Salah — AWS DMS tidak mendukung DynamoDB sebagai sumber CDC."],"k":"DynamoDB changes + banyak consumer / retensi > 24 jam → Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB."},{"id":"E1C-09","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Step Functions Distributed Map","q":"An AWS Step Functions workflow must process 500,000 small JSON objects that are stored in an Amazon S3 prefix by invoking an AWS Lambda function for each group of objects. The workflow must process objects with high parallelism, continue if a small percentage of items fail, and report which items failed. Which solution is the MOST scalable?","o":["Use an Inline Map state that iterates over a list of object keys passed in the execution input.","Use a single Lambda function that lists the prefix and processes all objects in a loop.","Use a Distributed Map state with an S3 ItemReader, an ItemBatcher to group objects, a tolerated failure percentage, and a ResultWriter that writes results to Amazon S3.","Use a Parallel state with one branch for each object key."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya '500,000 objects', 'high parallelism', 'continue if a small percentage fail', dan 'report which items failed' dengan syarat 'MOST scalable'. Distributed Map dapat membaca item langsung dari S3 (ItemReader), menjalankan hingga 10.000 child workflow paralel, mengelompokkan item dengan ItemBatcher, mentoleransi persentase kegagalan, dan menulis hasil termasuk item gagal ke S3 lewat ResultWriter. Distractor terdekat adalah Inline Map: konkurensinya terbatas (dokumentasi: hingga 40 iterasi bersamaan), daftar key harus muat di payload 256 KiB, dan riwayat eksekusi dibatasi 25.000 event. Satu Lambda yang memproses semuanya terbentur timeout 15 menit. Parallel state dipakai untuk cabang berbeda yang tetap jumlahnya, bukan ratusan ribu item. Aturan umum: jutaan objek S3 secara paralel di Step Functions → Distributed Map.","r":["Salah — Inline Map terbatas konkurensinya dan input daftar key melampaui batas payload 256 KiB serta batas riwayat eksekusi.","Salah — Satu Lambda terkena timeout 15 menit dan tidak paralel.","Benar — Distributed Map dirancang untuk skala besar dari S3, dengan batching, toleransi kegagalan, dan laporan hasil ke S3.","Salah — Parallel state untuk cabang statis yang berbeda, bukan untuk ratusan ribu item dinamis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'large-scale parallel processing of S3 objects' di Step Functions → Distributed Map (hingga 10.000 child executions)."},{"id":"E4A-57","d":4,"ts":"4.2.6","t":"Least-privilege DynamoDB policy with GSI","q":"An AWS Lambda function must run Query operations on the Amazon DynamoDB table Orders and on its global secondary index by-customer. The function must not be able to read or modify any other table or perform write operations. Which IAM policy statement follows the principle of least privilege and allows the function to work?","o":["Allow dynamodb:* on arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:111122223333:table/Orders.","Attach the AWS managed policy AmazonDynamoDBReadOnlyAccess.","Allow dynamodb:Query on arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:111122223333:table/Orders and arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:111122223333:table/Orders/index/by-customer.","Allow dynamodb:Query on arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:111122223333:table/Orders only."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: Query pada tabel 'and on its global secondary index' serta 'must not ... perform write operations'. Di DynamoDB, index memiliki ARN sendiri (table/Orders/index/nama-index), sehingga Query ke GSI ditolak bila policy hanya mencantumkan ARN tabel. Policy least privilege yang benar hanya mengizinkan dynamodb:Query pada ARN tabel dan ARN index yang dibutuhkan. dynamodb:* pada tabel mengizinkan penulisan dan penghapusan. AmazonDynamoDBReadOnlyAccess memberi akses baca ke semua tabel. ARN tabel saja tampak minimal, tetapi query ke index by-customer akan gagal. Aturan umum: least privilege = action spesifik + resource ARN spesifik, termasuk sub-resource seperti index.","r":["Salah — dynamodb:* mengizinkan operasi tulis dan hapus pada tabel.","Salah — Managed policy ini memberi akses baca ke semua tabel di akun.","Benar — Hanya Query pada ARN tabel dan ARN GSI yang diperlukan.","Salah — Query ke GSI membutuhkan ARN index; tanpa itu query ke by-customer ditolak."],"k":"Tips ujian: Query ke GSI butuh ARN table/NAME/index/INDEX di Resource; jangan pakai dynamodb:*."},{"id":"E1C-55","d":1,"ts":"1.4.3","t":"Redshift distribution and sort keys","q":"In Amazon Redshift, a 4-billion-row sales table and a 300-million-row customers table are frequently joined on customer_id, and most queries filter sales on a sale_date range. EXPLAIN shows DS_DIST_BOTH redistribution steps on the join and full scans of the sales table. Which combination of changes will improve query performance the MOST? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Set customer_id as the distribution key (DISTKEY) on both tables so joined rows are co-located on the same slices.","Set DISTSTYLE ALL on the 4-billion-row sales table.","Define sale_date as the sort key on the sales table so that zone maps can skip blocks outside the date range.","Run VACUUM DELETE ONLY on the customers table every hour.","Convert both tables to DISTSTYLE EVEN."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Dua masalah terlihat di EXPLAIN: 'DS_DIST_BOTH redistribution' pada join dan 'full scans' untuk filter tanggal. Menjadikan customer_id sebagai DISTKEY di kedua tabel menempatkan baris dengan customer_id yang sama pada slice yang sama, sehingga join tidak perlu memindahkan data antar node (DS_DIST_NONE). Sort key sale_date membuat zone maps (metadata min/max per blok) dapat melewati blok di luar rentang tanggal, sehingga pemindaian berkurang. Distractor terdekat adalah DISTSTYLE ALL pada tabel sales: menyalin 4 miliar baris ke setiap node sangat boros penyimpanan dan memperlambat load; ALL cocok untuk tabel dimensi kecil. DISTSTYLE EVEN tetap memerlukan redistribusi saat join. VACUUM tidak mengatasi pola distribusi. Aturan umum: join besar-besar → DISTKEY pada kolom join; filter rentang → SORTKEY.","r":["Benar — DISTKEY yang sama pada kolom join menghindari redistribusi data saat join.","Salah — ALL pada tabel fakta raksasa memboroskan penyimpanan dan memperlambat penulisan.","Benar — Sort key pada sale_date memungkinkan zone maps melewati blok di luar rentang.","Salah — VACUUM tidak mengubah distribusi atau mengurangi redistribusi.","Salah — EVEN tidak mengoptimalkan join dan tetap memicu redistribusi."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift DS_DIST_BOTH → DISTKEY pada kolom join; filter tanggal → SORTKEY."},{"id":"E2A-32","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"AWS Transfer Family","q":"A company receives daily CSV files from 40 external partners. The partners can send files only over SFTP using their existing clients and SSH keys. The files must land in an Amazon S3 bucket for downstream processing. The company does not want to manage any servers. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run an SFTP server on an Amazon EC2 instance in an Auto Scaling group and sync files to Amazon S3 with a cron job.","Use AWS DataSync agents installed at each partner location to copy files to Amazon S3.","Create an AWS Transfer Family server with the SFTP protocol and Amazon S3 as the storage backend.","Give each partner IAM user credentials and ask them to upload with the AWS CLI."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah partner 'can send files only over SFTP using their existing clients and SSH keys', tujuan 'Amazon S3', dan 'does not want to manage any servers'. AWS Transfer Family menyediakan endpoint SFTP (juga FTPS, FTP, dan AS2) yang fully managed, dengan autentikasi berbasis SSH key per pengguna dan penyimpanan langsung ke S3 atau EFS. Partner tidak perlu mengubah apa pun di sisi mereka. Distraktor terdekat adalah SFTP server di EC2: bisa memenuhi protokol, tetapi melanggar syarat tanpa server dan menambah patching serta skrip sinkronisasi. DataSync membutuhkan agent di lokasi sumber, yang tidak bisa dipaksakan ke partner eksternal. AWS CLI berarti partner harus mengganti tool dan mengelola kredensial IAM. Aturan umum: partner eksternal dengan SFTP/FTPS/AS2 ke S3 → AWS Transfer Family.","r":["Salah — Server SFTP di EC2 harus dikelola (patching, scaling, sinkronisasi) sehingga melanggar syarat tanpa server.","Salah — DataSync memerlukan agent di lokasi sumber dan tidak menyediakan endpoint SFTP untuk partner.","Benar — Transfer Family menyediakan endpoint SFTP managed dengan autentikasi SSH key dan langsung menyimpan file di S3.","Salah — Partner hanya bisa memakai SFTP; memaksa AWS CLI dan kredensial IAM mengubah proses mereka."],"k":"External partners + SFTP/FTPS/AS2 → AWS Transfer Family (S3 or EFS backend)."},{"id":"E4B-44","d":4,"ts":"4.5.2","t":"Macie with Lake Formation","q":"A data lake uses AWS Lake Formation with LF-Tag-based access control. Analysts are granted access to all columns that are not tagged Classification=PII. The company wants newly ingested data to be scanned for PII by Amazon Macie, and any table found to contain PII must automatically be protected so that analysts lose access to it. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure Amazon Macie to automatically revoke Lake Formation permissions when it generates a finding.","Move all newly ingested objects to a quarantine bucket until a data steward reviews them manually.","Send Macie findings to Amazon EventBridge, and invoke an AWS Lambda function that maps the affected S3 object to its Data Catalog table and assigns the LF-Tag Classification=PII to that table or its affected columns.","Create an AWS Config rule that checks whether S3 buckets contain PII."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: Macie mendeteksi PII lalu tabel harus 'automatically be protected' melalui Lake Formation LF-Tag. Macie tidak terintegrasi langsung untuk mengubah izin Lake Formation, tetapi Macie mempublikasikan findings ke Amazon EventBridge. Rule EventBridge dapat memicu Lambda yang memetakan lokasi S3 pada finding ke tabel Data Catalog dan menempelkan LF-Tag Classification=PII; karena izin analis berbasis tag, akses ke data tersebut otomatis hilang. Ini adalah pola umum 'Macie + Lake Formation' untuk PII identification. Distraktor terdekat adalah karantina manual: aman, tetapi tidak otomatis dan memperlambat ingestion. Macie tidak memiliki fitur bawaan untuk mencabut izin Lake Formation. AWS Config tidak memindai isi objek untuk PII. Aturan umum: deteksi PII (Macie) → otomatisasi via EventBridge → klasifikasi/izin di Lake Formation (LF-Tags).","r":["Salah — Macie tidak memiliki fitur bawaan untuk mencabut izin Lake Formation.","Salah — Karantina manual tidak otomatis dan memperlambat ketersediaan data.","Benar — EventBridge + Lambda menerapkan LF-Tag PII berdasarkan findings Macie sehingga izin berbasis tag langsung berlaku.","Salah — AWS Config mengevaluasi konfigurasi resource, bukan isi objek."],"k":"Tips ujian: Macie findings → EventBridge → Lambda → LF-Tag PII → Lake Formation TBAC menegakkan akses."},{"id":"E2B-56","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"Redshift cross-Region snapshot copy","q":"A company runs its enterprise data warehouse on an Amazon Redshift RA3 provisioned cluster in eu-west-1. The disaster recovery plan requires that the warehouse can be restored in eu-central-1 if eu-west-1 is unavailable, with an RPO of a few hours. The company wants the solution with the LEAST operational overhead. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Configure cross-Region snapshot copy on the cluster so that automated and manual snapshots are copied to eu-central-1, and restore from them during a disaster.","Run UNLOAD for all tables to Amazon S3 every night and replicate the bucket to eu-central-1.","Create a second Redshift cluster in eu-central-1 and run the same ETL jobs on both clusters.","Enable Multi-AZ on the cluster in eu-west-1."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'restored in eu-central-1 if eu-west-1 is unavailable', 'RPO of a few hours' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Redshift mendukung cross-Region snapshot copy: setelah dikonfigurasi, snapshot otomatis (biasanya setiap sekitar 8 jam atau per 5 GB perubahan) dan manual disalin ke Region tujuan, dan Anda bisa me-restore cluster dari snapshot tersebut saat bencana. Ini tidak memerlukan pipeline tambahan. UNLOAD malam hari ditambah replikasi butuh proses load ulang yang panjang saat bencana dan banyak pekerjaan. Cluster kedua dengan dual ETL mahal dan berat dipelihara. Multi-AZ melindungi dari kegagalan AZ, bukan kegagalan Region. Ingat: Redshift DR lintas Region → cross-Region snapshot copy; kegagalan AZ → Multi-AZ atau relocation.","r":["Benar — Cross-Region snapshot copy menyalin snapshot otomatis ke Region DR dan memungkinkan restore dengan overhead minimal.","Salah — UNLOAD dan replikasi membutuhkan pipeline kustom dan load ulang yang lama saat pemulihan.","Salah — Menjalankan dua cluster dan dua ETL menggandakan biaya dan kompleksitas.","Salah — Multi-AZ hanya melindungi dari kegagalan AZ dalam Region yang sama."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift DR ke Region lain → cross-Region snapshot copy."},{"id":"E1A-55","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"Kinesis hot shards and partition keys","q":"A Kinesis data stream with 20 shards ingests IoT readings. Producers use the device model as the partition key, and there are only 3 device models. Producers receive ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors even though total throughput is far below the stream's aggregate capacity. Which change will MOST effectively resolve the issue?","o":["Increase the number of shards to 40.","Enable server-side encryption on the stream.","Increase the stream's data retention period.","Use a high-cardinality partition key, such as the device ID, so that records are distributed evenly across shards."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: partition key 'device model' dengan 'only 3' nilai, dan throttling walau total throughput 'far below the aggregate capacity'. Kinesis memetakan partition key ke shard melalui hash; dengan hanya 3 nilai key, data hanya masuk ke paling banyak 3 dari 20 shard (hot shards), dan setiap shard dibatasi 1 MB/s atau 1.000 record/s untuk tulis. Mengganti ke key dengan kardinalitas tinggi seperti device ID menyebarkan beban ke semua shard. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah shard: tetap hanya 3 shard yang dipakai, sehingga throttling berlanjut dan biaya naik. Retensi dan enkripsi tidak memengaruhi distribusi tulis. Aturan umum: throttling Kinesis padahal kapasitas total cukup = hot shard karena partition key berkardinalitas rendah.","r":["Salah — Dengan 3 nilai key, shard tambahan tidak terpakai; hot shard tetap terjadi.","Salah — Enkripsi tidak mengubah distribusi data antar-shard.","Salah — Retensi tidak memengaruhi throughput tulis per shard.","Benar — Partition key berkardinalitas tinggi menyebarkan record merata ke semua shard."],"k":"Kinesis throttled tapi total kapasitas cukup → hot shard → partition key kardinalitas tinggi."},{"id":"E4A-07","d":4,"ts":"4.1.2","t":"Gateway vs interface VPC endpoints","q":"AWS Glue ETL jobs run in private subnets that have no NAT gateway and no internet gateway. The jobs must read and write data in Amazon S3 and retrieve database credentials from AWS Secrets Manager. Company policy forbids any traffic to the internet. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create a gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 and associate it with the route tables of the private subnets.","Create a NAT gateway in a public subnet and route the private subnets' traffic through it.","Create a gateway VPC endpoint for AWS Secrets Manager and add it to the route tables.","Create an interface VPC endpoint for AWS Secrets Manager with private DNS enabled, and allow HTTPS from the Glue security group in the endpoint's security group.","Create a VPC peering connection to the AWS Secrets Manager service VPC."],"a":[0,3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'no NAT gateway', 'forbids any traffic to the internet'. Amazon S3 (dan DynamoDB) mendukung gateway VPC endpoint yang gratis dan bekerja lewat entri di route table. Secrets Manager tidak punya gateway endpoint; aksesnya secara privat harus melalui interface VPC endpoint (AWS PrivateLink), yang berupa ENI dengan security group sendiri. Dengan private DNS aktif, SDK di Glue otomatis memakai endpoint privat tanpa perubahan kode, asalkan security group endpoint mengizinkan HTTPS 443 dari Glue. NAT gateway berarti traffic keluar ke internet sehingga melanggar kebijakan. VPC peering ke service AWS tidak dimungkinkan. Aturan umum: gateway endpoint hanya untuk S3 dan DynamoDB; service lain memakai interface endpoint (PrivateLink).","r":["Benar — Gateway endpoint S3 memberi akses privat ke S3 tanpa internet dan tanpa biaya per jam.","Salah — NAT gateway mengalirkan traffic ke internet, melanggar kebijakan perusahaan.","Salah — Secrets Manager tidak mendukung gateway endpoint; hanya S3 dan DynamoDB.","Benar — Interface endpoint Secrets Manager dengan private DNS memberi akses privat, dan security group endpoint harus mengizinkan 443 dari Glue.","Salah — Tidak ada mekanisme VPC peering ke VPC milik service AWS."],"k":"Tips ujian: gateway endpoint = S3 dan DynamoDB saja; service lain (Secrets Manager, KMS, Glue, STS) = interface endpoint/PrivateLink."},{"id":"E1C-70","d":1,"ts":"1.4.6","t":"AWS SAM local testing","q":"A data engineer is developing an AWS Lambda function that is triggered by Amazon S3 object-created events and is defined in an AWS SAM template. Before deploying, the engineer wants to run the function on a laptop with a realistic S3 event payload to debug the parsing logic. Which approach meets this requirement?","o":["Use 'sam local generate-event s3 put' to create a sample event and run 'sam local invoke' with that event file.","Deploy the function to production and upload a test file to the bucket.","Run 'sam deploy --guided' and check the CloudFormation events.","Use 'cdk diff' to compare the function code with the deployed version."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: menjalankan fungsi 'on a laptop' dengan 'realistic S3 event payload' sebelum deploy. AWS SAM CLI menyediakan 'sam local generate-event' untuk membuat payload contoh berbagai layanan (termasuk S3 put) dan 'sam local invoke' untuk menjalankan fungsi secara lokal dalam container yang meniru runtime Lambda. Distractor terdekat adalah menguji di produksi: payload memang nyata, tetapi melanggar syarat sebelum deploy dan berisiko. 'sam deploy --guided' men-deploy, bukan menguji lokal. 'cdk diff' membandingkan perubahan infrastruktur CDK, bukan menjalankan kode. Aturan umum: debugging Lambda lokal dengan SAM → sam local generate-event + sam local invoke (atau sam local start-api untuk API).","r":["Benar — SAM CLI membuat event S3 contoh dan menjalankan fungsi secara lokal dalam container runtime Lambda.","Salah — Menguji di produksi berisiko dan tidak dilakukan sebelum deploy.","Salah — Perintah ini men-deploy aplikasi, bukan menjalankan fungsi lokal.","Salah — cdk diff menampilkan perbedaan infrastruktur, bukan menjalankan kode."],"k":"Tips ujian: test Lambda locally → sam local invoke (dengan sam local generate-event)."},{"id":"E2B-32","d":2,"ts":"2.3.1","t":"Redshift COPY with manifest","q":"A data engineer loads a nightly batch of exactly 25 files into Amazon Redshift. The files are written to an S3 prefix that also contains files from other systems. The load must include only those 25 files, and it must fail if any of them is missing instead of silently loading a partial batch. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run COPY with the prefix and the MAXERROR 0 option.","Use a COPY command with a manifest file that lists the 25 files, and mark each entry as mandatory.","Run COPY with the prefix and the NOLOAD option, and then run it again without NOLOAD.","Use COPY with the ACCEPTINVCHARS option so that unexpected files are skipped."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'include only those 25 files' di prefix yang berisi file lain, dan 'fail if any of them is missing'. COPY dengan MANIFEST membaca file JSON yang mencantumkan URL S3 setiap file secara eksplisit, sehingga file lain di prefix tidak ikut dimuat. Setiap entri bisa diberi 'mandatory': true; jika file tersebut tidak ditemukan, COPY gagal alih-alih memuat sebagian. MAXERROR 0 mengatur toleransi error per baris, bukan file yang hilang, dan COPY berbasis prefix tetap memuat file lain. NOLOAD hanya memvalidasi data tanpa memuat. ACCEPTINVCHARS mengganti karakter UTF-8 yang tidak valid. Ingat: 'load exactly these files' atau 'fail if file missing' → COPY dengan manifest + mandatory.","r":["Salah — MAXERROR mengatur error baris; COPY berbasis prefix tetap memuat file dari sistem lain.","Benar — Manifest membatasi file yang dimuat, dan mandatory membuat COPY gagal jika ada file yang hilang.","Salah — NOLOAD hanya validasi; COPY berbasis prefix tetap mengambil file yang tidak diinginkan.","Salah — ACCEPTINVCHARS menangani karakter tidak valid, bukan pemilihan file."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'specific files' / 'fail if a file is missing' → COPY ... MANIFEST dengan mandatory=true."},{"id":"E2A-21","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"DynamoDB key design for time series","q":"A company stores temperature readings from 100,000 devices in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The most frequent request is to fetch the 10 most recent readings for a given device. Which table design and access method should a data engineer use?","o":["Partition key timestamp and sort key device_id; run a Scan with a Limit of 10.","Partition key device_id and sort key reading_timestamp; run a Query with ScanIndexForward set to false and Limit set to 10.","Partition key device_id with no sort key; run a Scan with a FilterExpression on device_id.","Partition key reading_timestamp with no sort key; create a GSI on device_id and run a Scan on the GSI."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'fetch the 10 most recent readings for a given device'. Dengan device_id sebagai partition key dan reading_timestamp sebagai sort key, semua pembacaan satu perangkat berada dalam satu item collection yang sudah terurut berdasarkan waktu. Operasi Query dengan ScanIndexForward=false membaca dari timestamp terbaru, dan Limit=10 menghentikan pembacaan setelah 10 item, sehingga hemat RCU dan latensi rendah. Distraktor terdekat adalah device_id tanpa sort key: setiap perangkat hanya bisa menyimpan satu item, dan Scan memindai seluruh tabel. Timestamp sebagai partition key membuat query per perangkat mustahil tanpa Scan. Aturan umum: 'latest N items per entity' di DynamoDB → partition key = entity, sort key = timestamp, Query dengan ScanIndexForward=false.","r":["Salah — Scan dengan Limit hanya mengambil 10 item pertama yang dibaca dari tabel, bukan 10 terbaru untuk perangkat tertentu.","Benar — Query pada device_id dengan urutan menurun berdasarkan timestamp dan Limit 10 mengambil tepat data terbaru dengan efisien.","Salah — Tanpa sort key hanya ada satu item per device_id, dan Scan memindai seluruh tabel.","Salah — Scan pada GSI tetap memindai seluruh index; desain ini juga tidak mengurutkan berdasarkan waktu per perangkat."],"k":"Latest N per entity → PK = entity, SK = timestamp, Query + ScanIndexForward=false + Limit."},{"id":"E1A-63","d":1,"ts":"1.1.10","t":"EventBridge cross-account event buses","q":"A company has 10 application accounts that emit order events to their default Amazon EventBridge event buses. A central data account must receive all of these events on a single event bus and route them to several targets, such as an Amazon Data Firehose stream and an AWS Step Functions state machine. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Create an Amazon SQS queue in each application account and poll them from the central account.","Enable AWS CloudTrail in every account and parse the logs in the central account.","Add a resource-based policy to the central account's event bus that allows the 10 application accounts to put events.","Create one Firehose stream per application account in the central account.","In each application account, create an EventBridge rule that matches the order events and targets the central account's event bus."],"a":[2,4],"e":"Kata kunci: event dari '10 application accounts' ke 'single event bus' di akun pusat (fan-in), lalu diteruskan ke 'several targets' (fan-out). EventBridge mendukung pengiriman event lintas akun: event bus pusat membutuhkan resource-based policy yang mengizinkan akun-akun sumber melakukan PutEvents, dan di setiap akun sumber dibuat rule yang memfilter event order dengan target event bus pusat. Di akun pusat, rule tambahan dapat mengirim event yang sama ke banyak target. Distraktor terdekat adalah SQS per akun dengan polling dari pusat: berfungsi, tetapi menambah kode dan komponen. CloudTrail mencatat API call, bukan event bisnis aplikasi. Satu Firehose per akun tidak memusatkan event ke satu bus. Aturan umum: fan-in event lintas akun = rule di akun sumber → event bus pusat dengan resource policy; fan-out = banyak rule/target di bus pusat.","r":["Salah — Polling SQS lintas akun menambah kode dan komponen yang tidak perlu.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan event bisnis aplikasi.","Benar — Resource-based policy pada bus pusat mengizinkan akun sumber mengirim event.","Salah — Tidak memusatkan event ke satu bus dan menambah banyak stream.","Benar — Rule di setiap akun sumber meneruskan event order ke event bus pusat."],"k":"Fan-in EventBridge lintas akun → rule di akun sumber target bus pusat + resource policy di bus pusat."},{"id":"E2A-43","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Aurora zero-ETL integration with Redshift","q":"A company runs an order application on Amazon Aurora MySQL. The analytics team needs the order data replicated into Amazon Redshift continuously with near-real-time latency to run heavy analytical queries. The company does not want to build or operate ETL pipelines and does not want analytical queries to add load to the Aurora database. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Redshift federated queries against the Aurora MySQL database for all analytical queries.","Create an Aurora zero-ETL integration with Amazon Redshift.","Schedule an AWS Glue job every 5 minutes to extract changed rows from Aurora and load them into Redshift.","Export Aurora snapshots to Amazon S3 daily and query them with Redshift Spectrum."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'replicated ... continuously with near-real-time latency', 'does not want to build or operate ETL pipelines', dan 'does not want analytical queries to add load to the Aurora database'. Aurora zero-ETL integration dengan Amazon Redshift mereplikasi data transaksional ke Redshift secara otomatis dalam hitungan detik, tanpa pipeline yang perlu dikelola; query analitik berat dijalankan di Redshift sehingga tidak membebani Aurora. Distraktor terdekat adalah federated query: tanpa ETL, tetapi setiap query analitik membaca langsung dari Aurora sehingga menambah beban ke database operasional. Glue job per 5 menit adalah pipeline ETL yang ingin dihindari. Ekspor snapshot harian terlalu lambat. Aturan umum: replikasi berkelanjutan OLTP (Aurora/RDS/DynamoDB) ke Redshift tanpa ETL → zero-ETL integration; akses data live sesekali → federated query.","r":["Salah — Federated query menjalankan pembacaan pada Aurora sehingga query analitik berat membebani database operasional.","Benar — Zero-ETL integration mereplikasi data Aurora ke Redshift dalam near-real-time tanpa pipeline yang dikelola.","Salah — Glue job terjadwal adalah pipeline ETL yang harus dibangun dan dipelihara.","Salah — Ekspor snapshot harian tidak memenuhi kebutuhan near-real-time."],"k":"Aurora → Redshift continuous, no ETL, offload analytics → zero-ETL integration."},{"id":"E3A-43","d":3,"ts":"3.2.4","t":"Athena for Apache Spark notebooks","q":"A data analyst wants to interactively explore 3 TB of Parquet data in Amazon S3 with PySpark, iterating on code cell by cell and visualizing intermediate results. The analyst explores only a few hours per week and does not want to provision, configure, or remember to shut down any cluster. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Launch an Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster with JupyterHub each time and terminate it after the session.","Create an AWS Glue ETL job and rerun it after every code change.","Use an Amazon Athena workgroup with the Apache Spark engine and explore the data in an Athena notebook.","Run Apache Spark in local mode on a large Amazon EC2 instance with Jupyter installed."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'interactively explore with PySpark', 'cell by cell', 'few hours per week', dan 'not provision or shut down any cluster'. Amazon Athena for Apache Spark menyediakan notebook yang kompatibel dengan Jupyter di atas engine Spark serverless; session dimulai dalam hitungan detik, kapasitas (DPU) dikelola Athena, dan session berakhir otomatis setelah idle timeout. Data di S3 dan tabel di Glue Data Catalog bisa langsung dibaca. Cluster EMR on EC2 dengan JupyterHub harus dibuat, dikonfigurasi, dan dimatikan sendiri. Glue ETL job adalah batch, bukan eksplorasi interaktif sel per sel. Spark local mode di EC2 tidak skala untuk 3 TB dan instance harus dikelola. Catatan: notebook di konsol Athena tersedia pada release PySpark engine version 3; release Apache Spark 3.5 dipakai dari notebook SageMaker Unified Studio. Aturan umum: eksplorasi interaktif PySpark serverless → Athena notebook dengan Apache Spark.","r":["Salah — Cluster harus dibuat, dikonfigurasi, dan dimatikan sendiri sehingga overhead tinggi.","Salah — Glue ETL job adalah batch, tidak interaktif sel per sel.","Benar — Athena for Apache Spark menyediakan notebook serverless yang cepat mulai dan otomatis berhenti saat idle.","Salah — Satu instance tidak skala untuk 3 TB dan harus dikelola sendiri."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'interactive PySpark, serverless, start in seconds' → Athena notebooks (Apache Spark engine)."},{"id":"E2B-43","d":2,"ts":"2.3.3","t":"Retaining a number of noncurrent versions","q":"A versioned S3 bucket stores configuration snapshots for data pipelines. Objects are overwritten many times per day. The team must be able to roll back to any of the 5 most recent previous versions of each object, but older versions must be deleted automatically to control cost. Which Lifecycle configuration meets these requirements?","o":["A NoncurrentVersionExpiration action with NewerNoncurrentVersions set to 5 and NoncurrentDays set to 1.","An Expiration action of 5 days for current versions.","A NoncurrentVersionTransition action to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 5 days.","An S3 Object Lock retention period of 5 days in governance mode."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'roll back to any of the 5 most recent previous versions' dan 'older versions must be deleted automatically'. NoncurrentVersionExpiration mendukung NewerNoncurrentVersions: S3 mempertahankan N versi noncurrent terbaru dan hanya menghapus versi yang lebih lama setelah NoncurrentDays. Dengan nilai 5, selalu ada 5 versi sebelumnya untuk rollback. Expiration pada versi current hanya membuat delete marker dan tidak membatasi jumlah versi. Transisi noncurrent ke Glacier tidak menghapus versi dan membuat rollback lambat. Object Lock justru mencegah penghapusan. Ingat: 'keep last N versions' → NewerNoncurrentVersions di NoncurrentVersionExpiration.","r":["Benar — NewerNoncurrentVersions = 5 menyimpan lima versi terbaru dan menghapus sisanya secara otomatis.","Salah — Expiration versi current hanya menambah delete marker dan tidak membatasi jumlah versi lama.","Salah — Transisi tidak menghapus versi, sehingga biaya tetap bertambah dan rollback menjadi lambat.","Salah — Object Lock mencegah penghapusan, kebalikan dari kebutuhan membersihkan versi lama."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'retain only the last N versions' → NoncurrentVersionExpiration + NewerNoncurrentVersions."},{"id":"E3A-08","d":3,"ts":"3.1.2","t":"Troubleshooting Step Functions and Glue concurrency","q":"An AWS Step Functions workflow is triggered once for each file that arrives in Amazon S3. Each execution starts the same AWS Glue job with the .sync pattern. When many files arrive at once, some executions fail with Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException. The pipeline must process every file without manual reruns. Which TWO actions will resolve the issue? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Add a Retry on the Glue task for Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException with an interval and exponential backoff.","Change the Glue job worker type from G.1X to G.2X.","Increase the Maximum concurrency setting of the Glue job to a value that supports the expected number of parallel runs.","Add a Catch that sends the error to Amazon SNS and ends the execution.","Convert the Step Functions workflow from Standard to Express."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Error Glue.ConcurrentRunsExceededException berarti jumlah run paralel melebihi pengaturan 'Maximum concurrency' Glue job (default 1). Ada dua cara yang saling melengkapi: naikkan Maximum concurrency job ke angka yang sesuai beban paralel, dan tambahkan Retry khusus error itu dengan backoff agar eksekusi yang tetap tertolak akan dicoba lagi otomatis, sesuai syarat 'without manual reruns'. Mengganti worker type ke G.2X menambah memori/CPU per worker tetapi tidak mengubah batas jumlah run paralel. Catch ke SNS hanya memberi tahu kegagalan, file tetap tidak diproses. Express workflow tidak mendukung .sync dan tidak menyentuh akar masalah. Aturan umum: baca nama error di execution history Step Functions untuk menemukan akar masalah, lalu gunakan Retry untuk error yang bersifat sementara.","r":["Benar — Retry dengan backoff mengulang otomatis ketika slot concurrency Glue sedang penuh.","Salah — Worker type yang lebih besar tidak mengubah batas jumlah run paralel.","Benar — Maximum concurrency yang lebih tinggi menghilangkan penyebab error saat banyak file tiba bersamaan.","Salah — Catch ke SNS hanya memberi notifikasi; file tetap gagal diproses dan perlu rerun manual.","Salah — Express workflow tidak mendukung pola .sync dan tidak menyelesaikan batas concurrency."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ConcurrentRunsExceededException' → naikkan Maximum concurrency Glue job + Retry dengan backoff."},{"id":"E2B-20","d":2,"ts":"2.2.4","t":"Glue partition indexes","q":"A Data Catalog table holds 3 million partitions with keys region, dt, and customer_id. The table is queried by Amazon Athena, Amazon Redshift Spectrum, and AWS Glue ETL jobs. Queries that filter on region and dt spend most of their time in the GetPartitions call before any data is read. Which solution will reduce query planning time while keeping the table usable by all three services?","o":["Enable Athena partition projection for all three partition keys.","Create an AWS Glue partition index on the region and dt keys.","Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE before each query to refresh the partitions.","Move the table into a separate Data Catalog database for each region."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'GetPartitions' lambat pada tabel dengan 3 juta partisi, filter pada 'region and dt', dan tabel harus tetap dipakai 'Athena, Redshift Spectrum, and AWS Glue ETL'. Glue partition index membuat indeks atas subset kunci partisi sehingga Data Catalog bisa mengembalikan hanya partisi yang cocok dengan filter, tanpa memuat semua partisi. Indeks ini dimanfaatkan oleh Athena, Redshift Spectrum dan Glue, sehingga semua konsumen tetap bisa memakai tabel. Partition projection memang mempercepat Athena, tetapi hanya Athena yang memahaminya, sehingga Spectrum dan Glue akan bermasalah. MSCK REPAIR sebelum query justru menambah waktu. Memecah database per region menambah kompleksitas tanpa memperbaiki lookup partisi. Ingat: banyak partisi + banyak engine → partition index; Athena-only → partition projection.","r":["Salah — Partition projection hanya dipahami Athena; Spectrum dan Glue ETL tidak bisa memakainya.","Benar — Partition index mempercepat pencarian partisi berdasarkan region dan dt untuk semua layanan yang memakai Data Catalog.","Salah — MSCK REPAIR menambah partisi yang belum terdaftar, bukan mempercepat lookup, dan memperlambat setiap query.","Salah — Memecah database menambah objek yang harus dikelola dan tidak menyelesaikan masalah GetPartitions."],"k":"Tips ujian: GetPartitions lambat + multi-engine → Glue partition indexes."},{"id":"E3B-32","d":3,"ts":"3.3.4","t":"Redshift query monitoring rules","q":"Analysts sometimes submit poorly written ad hoc queries to an Amazon Redshift cluster that create large nested loop joins and consume most cluster resources. A data engineer wants Redshift to automatically cancel, and record in a system table, any query in the ad hoc queue whose nested loop join row count exceeds 1 billion rows. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Set the statement_timeout parameter to 30 minutes for all users.","Define a query monitoring rule (QMR) in the WLM configuration for the ad hoc queue with the predicate nested_loop_join_row_count > 1000000000 and the abort action.","Review Amazon Redshift Advisor recommendations every week.","Create a CloudWatch alarm on CPUUtilization that reboots the cluster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'automatically', 'nested loop join row count', serta 'cancel and record' untuk queue tertentu. Query monitoring rules (QMR) di WLM mendefinisikan hingga tiga predikat berbasis metrik query (seperti nested_loop_join_row_count, query_execution_time, scan_row_count) dan SATU aksi per rule: log, abort, hop (hanya manual WLM), atau change priority (hanya automatic WLM). Aksi abort juga mencatat aksinya di STL_WLM_RULE_ACTION sebelum membatalkan query, sehingga satu rule sudah memenuhi kedua kebutuhan. Distraktor terdekat adalah statement_timeout: hanya berdasarkan waktu, tidak bisa mendeteksi nested loop join, dan berlaku luas. Advisor memberi rekomendasi, bukan penegakan otomatis. Reboot cluster mengganggu semua pengguna. Aturan: kendalikan 'runaway queries' berdasarkan metrik → Redshift QMR.","r":["Salah — Timeout hanya berbasis durasi dan tidak bisa menargetkan kondisi nested loop join.","Benar — QMR mengevaluasi nested_loop_join_row_count per queue; aksi abort mencatat aksi ke STL_WLM_RULE_ACTION lalu membatalkan query secara otomatis.","Salah — Advisor hanya memberi rekomendasi, bukan tindakan otomatis terhadap query.","Salah — Reboot menghentikan semua pekerjaan dan tidak menargetkan query bermasalah."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'automatically abort/log queries that exceed X' di Redshift → QMR (hop = manual WLM, change priority = auto WLM)."},{"id":"E4B-22","d":4,"ts":"4.3.4","t":"Glue JDBC SSL","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job extracts data from an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database through a JDBC connection. A compliance review requires that the data be encrypted in transit between AWS Glue and the database, and the database must reject unencrypted connections from any client. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store the database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and reference the secret in the Glue connection.","Encrypt the RDS DB instance storage with a customer managed AWS KMS key.","Enable the 'Require SSL connection' option on the AWS Glue JDBC connection, and set the rds.force_ssl parameter to 1 in the DB parameter group.","Attach an AWS Glue security configuration with SSE-KMS encryption to the job."],"a":[2],"e":"Dua syarat menentukan: trafik Glue ↔ database 'encrypted in transit' dan database 'must reject unencrypted connections from any client'. Opsi 'Require SSL connection' pada Glue JDBC connection membuat Glue memakai SSL saat terhubung, sedangkan parameter rds.force_ssl = 1 pada RDS for PostgreSQL membuat database menolak koneksi non-SSL dari klien mana pun. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue security configuration: ini mengenkripsi data at rest yang ditulis job (S3, log, bookmark), bukan koneksi JDBC. Secrets Manager mengamankan kredensial, bukan mengenkripsi trafik. Enkripsi storage RDS adalah enkripsi at rest. Aturan umum: in transit ke database → SSL di sisi klien (Glue connection) + force SSL di sisi server (parameter group).","r":["Salah — Secrets Manager melindungi kredensial, bukan mengenkripsi data yang dikirim.","Salah — Enkripsi storage RDS hanya melindungi data at rest.","Benar — SSL di Glue connection dan rds.force_ssl di database memenuhi enkripsi in transit dan penolakan koneksi non-SSL.","Salah — Security configuration Glue mengenkripsi output/log/bookmark at rest, bukan koneksi JDBC."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue JDBC in transit → 'Require SSL connection'; server side enforce → rds.force_ssl / require_ssl."},{"id":"E4B-11","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"KMS key rotation and key policy","q":"A security team defines requirements for the AWS KMS key that encrypts a data lake. The key material must rotate automatically without any application changes. The administrators who manage the key must not automatically be able to decrypt data, and only the ETL roles must be able to use the key for encryption and decryption. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use the AWS managed key aws/s3 for the data lake buckets.","Create a symmetric customer managed key and enable automatic key rotation.","Create a customer managed key with imported key material and enable automatic key rotation.","Grant the key administrators the kms:* permission through their IAM policies.","Write a key policy that grants key management actions to the administrator role and grants only cryptographic actions such as kms:Encrypt, kms:Decrypt, and kms:GenerateDataKey to the ETL roles."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Ada dua kebutuhan: rotasi 'automatically without any application changes' dan pemisahan antara administrator kunci dan pengguna kunci. Customer managed key simetris mendukung automatic key rotation; KMS menyimpan material kunci lama sehingga data lama tetap bisa didekripsi dan aplikasi tidak perlu diubah. Pemisahan peran diatur melalui key policy: administrator diberi aksi manajemen (Create*, Describe*, Enable*, Put*, ScheduleKeyDeletion, dll.) tanpa aksi kriptografi, sedangkan role ETL hanya diberi Encrypt/Decrypt/GenerateDataKey. Distraktor terdekat adalah AWS managed key aws/s3: rotasinya otomatis, tetapi key policy-nya tidak dapat diubah sehingga Anda tidak bisa membatasi pengguna kunci. Imported key material tidak mendukung automatic rotation (harus rotasi manual). Memberi kms:* ke admin justru melanggar pemisahan tugas. Aturan umum: kontrol penuh + rotasi otomatis → customer managed key simetris + key policy yang memisahkan admin dan user.","r":["Salah — Key policy AWS managed key tidak bisa diubah sehingga pemisahan admin vs pengguna tidak dapat diterapkan.","Benar — Customer managed key simetris mendukung rotasi otomatis yang transparan bagi aplikasi.","Salah — Kunci dengan imported key material tidak mendukung automatic key rotation.","Salah — kms:* memberi admin kemampuan mendekripsi data, melanggar pemisahan tugas.","Benar — Key policy memisahkan izin manajemen kunci dari izin kriptografi untuk role ETL."],"k":"Tips ujian: imported key material/XKS → tidak ada automatic rotation; separation of duties → key policy admin vs key users."},{"id":"E1C-58","d":1,"ts":"1.4.4","t":"Testing Glue code locally","q":"A team wants to unit test the PySpark transformation logic of its AWS Glue jobs automatically on every pull request, before any code is deployed to AWS. Tests must use the same Glue libraries as the Glue runtime and must not incur charges for Glue job runs. Which approach meets these requirements?","o":["Deploy every change to the production Glue job and check the output manually.","Run each pull request's code as a Glue job in the development account and compare the outputs manually.","Write unit tests with pytest that run inside the official AWS Glue Docker image (for example, in an AWS CodeBuild project) against small sample DataFrames.","Rely on AWS Glue Data Quality rules in production to detect logic errors."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: unit test 'automatically on every pull request', 'before any code is deployed', memakai 'the same Glue libraries', dan 'must not incur charges for Glue job runs'. AWS menyediakan image Docker resmi AWS Glue yang berisi runtime Spark dan pustaka Glue (awsglue), sehingga tes pytest dapat dijalankan secara lokal atau di CodeBuild pada DataFrame contoh kecil, tanpa biaya Glue job run. Distractor terdekat adalah menjalankan job Glue di akun dev: menggunakan runtime yang sama, tetapi dikenai biaya DPU, lebih lambat, dan dicek manual. Pengujian di produksi melanggar syarat sebelum deploy. Glue Data Quality memeriksa kualitas data saat runtime, bukan menguji logika kode sebelum deploy. Aturan umum: unit test logika ETL secara lokal/CI dengan container Glue dan data sampel kecil; data quality rules melengkapi, bukan menggantikan.","r":["Salah — Pengujian di produksi berisiko dan tidak otomatis.","Salah — Menimbulkan biaya Glue job run dan pemeriksaan manual.","Benar — Image Docker Glue memberi pustaka yang sama, tes pytest berjalan otomatis di CI tanpa biaya job Glue.","Salah — Data Quality memvalidasi data di runtime, bukan menguji kode sebelum deploy."],"k":"Tips ujian: test Glue ETL lokal/CI → official AWS Glue Docker image + pytest."},{"id":"E2A-55","d":2,"ts":"2.1.7","t":"Iceberg partition evolution","q":"An Apache Iceberg table that stores web events is partitioned by month(event_ts). Event volume has grown 20x, and most queries now filter on a single day. The data engineer wants new data to be partitioned by day without rewriting the 3 years of existing data and without changing analysts' SQL queries. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a new table partitioned by day with CREATE TABLE AS SELECT, copy all historical data, and rename the tables.","Use Iceberg partition evolution to replace the month(event_ts) partition field with day(event_ts), for example with an ALTER TABLE ... REPLACE PARTITION FIELD statement in Spark.","Add a new event_day string column, populate it for new data, and ask analysts to filter on event_day.","Change the S3 prefix structure for new files to include the day and run an AWS Glue crawler."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'without rewriting the 3 years of existing data' dan 'without changing analysts' SQL queries'. Iceberg mendukung partition evolution: spesifikasi partisi dapat diubah sebagai operasi metadata, sehingga data lama tetap memakai partisi bulanan dan data baru memakai partisi harian, dan query planner menangani keduanya. Karena Iceberg memakai hidden partitioning (partisi diturunkan dari transformasi kolom seperti day(event_ts)), analis tetap memfilter pada event_ts dan partition pruning terjadi otomatis. Distraktor terdekat adalah CTAS ke tabel baru: menghasilkan partisi harian, tetapi menulis ulang seluruh data historis yang mahal dan lama. Menambah kolom event_day mengharuskan analis mengubah query, yang merupakan masalah klasik partisi gaya Hive. Mengubah prefix S3 tidak berpengaruh pada tabel Iceberg yang dilacak oleh metadata. Aturan umum: ubah granularitas partisi tanpa rewrite → Iceberg partition evolution + hidden partitioning.","r":["Salah — CTAS menulis ulang seluruh data historis, melanggar syarat tanpa rewrite.","Benar — Partition evolution mengubah spesifikasi partisi untuk data baru saja, dan hidden partitioning menjaga query analis tetap sama.","Salah — Kolom partisi eksplisit memaksa analis mengubah filter query mereka.","Salah — Iceberg melacak file melalui metadata, bukan struktur prefix, dan crawler tidak mengubah spesifikasi partisi."],"k":"Change partition granularity without rewrite or query changes → Iceberg partition evolution (hidden partitioning)."},{"id":"E2B-09","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler table grouping","q":"A data engineer points an AWS Glue crawler at s3://sales/orders/. The prefix contains one subfolder per country (for example, country=US/ and country=DE/). All files are JSON with the same core fields, but some countries add one or two optional fields. Instead of one partitioned 'orders' table, the crawler creates a separate table for each country folder. Analysts need one table that they can filter by country. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a separate crawler for each country and union the tables in an Amazon Athena view.","Add a custom JSON classifier with the JSON path '$[*]' to force all files into one table.","Enable the crawler option 'Create a single schema for each S3 path' so that compatible schemas are combined into one table with a country partition.","Set the crawler schema change policy to 'Ignore the change and don't update the table in the Data Catalog'."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'creates a separate table for each country folder' padahal skemanya hampir sama, dan analis butuh 'one table that they can filter by country'. Crawler membandingkan kemiripan skema antar folder; jika berbeda cukup jauh, setiap folder dianggap tabel sendiri. Opsi 'Create a single schema for each S3 path' (table grouping policy CombineCompatibleSchemas) memaksa crawler menggabungkan skema yang kompatibel menjadi satu tabel, dengan folder country= sebagai partisi dan field opsional sebagai kolom tambahan. Banyak crawler plus view union menambah objek dan pemeliharaan setiap ada negara baru. JSON classifier mengatur cara membaca struktur JSON, bukan cara pengelompokan tabel. Schema change policy hanya berlaku pada tabel yang sudah ada. Ingat: crawler membuat terlalu banyak tabel → gunakan opsi single schema per S3 path atau atur table level.","r":["Salah — Banyak crawler dan view union menambah overhead dan harus diubah setiap kali negara baru muncul.","Salah — JSON classifier mengatur path pembacaan record, bukan menggabungkan folder menjadi satu tabel.","Benar — Opsi single schema per S3 path menggabungkan skema kompatibel menjadi satu tabel berpartisi country.","Salah — Schema change policy tidak mencegah crawler membuat tabel terpisah per folder."],"k":"Tips ujian: crawler bikin banyak tabel kecil → 'Create a single schema for each S3 path' (CombineCompatibleSchemas) / table level."},{"id":"E1B-32","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"AWS Glue job bookmarks","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job runs every hour and reads all objects under an S3 prefix that keeps growing as new files are added. Each run reprocesses all historical files, so run time and cost increase every day. The output must contain each input record only once. Which solution will reduce cost MOST effectively?","o":["Increase the number of workers so that each run finishes faster.","Change the schedule from hourly to daily.","Add an S3 Lifecycle rule to move input files to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after one hour.","Enable AWS Glue job bookmarks so that each run processes only new files since the previous successful run."],"a":[3],"e":"Masalah utamanya adalah setiap run 'reprocesses all historical files' dan output harus berisi setiap record 'only once'. Job bookmark menyimpan state dari run sebelumnya sehingga Glue hanya membaca objek S3 baru, yang langsung memangkas waktu dan biaya serta mencegah duplikasi output. Menambah worker hanya mempercepat pemrosesan data yang sama, sehingga biaya DPU-hour tetap tumbuh. Mengubah jadwal ke harian mengurangi frekuensi tetapi tetap memproses ulang seluruh histori dan melanggar kebutuhan bisnis per jam. Memindahkan file ke Glacier membuat Glue tidak bisa membaca langsung file tersebut dan bukan cara mengelola pemrosesan inkremental. Aturan umum: pemrosesan inkremental di Glue → job bookmarks.","r":["Salah — Lebih banyak worker tidak mengurangi jumlah data yang diproses ulang, sehingga biaya tidak turun.","Salah — Tetap memproses ulang semua histori dan mengubah frekuensi bisnis.","Salah — Glacier membuat objek tidak langsung terbaca dan tidak memberi mekanisme inkremental.","Benar — Bookmark hanya memproses file baru, mengurangi biaya dan mencegah duplikasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'process only new data / avoid reprocessing in Glue' → job bookmarks."},{"id":"E3A-10","d":3,"ts":"3.1.3","t":"SDK pagination","q":"An AWS Lambda function written in Python uses Boto3 to list all objects under an Amazon S3 prefix and write an inventory file. The prefix contains about 40,000 objects, but the inventory file always contains exactly 1,000 entries. What is the MOST likely fix?","o":["Increase the memory of the Lambda function so that more objects can be returned.","Set the MaxKeys parameter of list_objects_v2 to 40,000.","Use a Boto3 paginator for list_objects_v2 (or loop with the ContinuationToken) to read every page of results.","Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on the bucket."],"a":[2],"e":"Angka 'exactly 1,000 entries' adalah petunjuk utama: ListObjectsV2 mengembalikan paling banyak 1.000 key per panggilan. Untuk membaca semuanya, gunakan paginator Boto3 (get_paginator('list_objects_v2')) atau loop manual dengan ContinuationToken sampai IsTruncated bernilai false. Menaikkan memori Lambda tidak mengubah ukuran halaman API. MaxKeys hanya bisa memperkecil halaman; nilai di atas 1.000 tetap dibatasi 1.000. Transfer Acceleration mempercepat transfer data jarak jauh dan tidak berhubungan dengan listing. Aturan umum: setiap API AWS yang mengembalikan daftar (S3, Glue GetTables, DynamoDB Scan, Athena GetQueryResults) bersifat paginated, jadi selalu gunakan paginator.","r":["Salah — Memori Lambda tidak memengaruhi jumlah key yang dikembalikan per panggilan API.","Salah — MaxKeys tidak bisa melebihi 1.000 per halaman.","Benar — Paginator atau ContinuationToken membaca semua halaman hasil sampai habis.","Salah — Transfer Acceleration hanya mempercepat upload/download, bukan listing objek."],"k":"Tips ujian: hasil 'tepat 1.000' dari S3 list → paginasi (paginator/ContinuationToken)."},{"id":"E1B-09","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Managed Service for Apache Flink vs MSK Connect","q":"A logistics company streams shipment status events through Amazon MSK. The company must continuously filter invalid events, enrich each event with stateful per-shipment information (for example, time since last scan), and write results to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Processing must tolerate failures without losing state, and the company does not want to manage servers. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink with checkpointing enabled to read from MSK, keep keyed state per shipment, and write to OpenSearch Service.","Use Amazon MSK Connect with the OpenSearch sink connector to deliver the events directly.","Use AWS Lambda with an MSK event source mapping and keep per-shipment state in Lambda function memory.","Use Amazon Data Firehose with MSK as the source and a Lambda transformation function to compute the time since the last scan."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratan yang menentukan adalah 'stateful per-shipment information', 'tolerate failures without losing state', dan tanpa mengelola server. Managed Service for Apache Flink menyimpan keyed state per kunci (per shipment), dan checkpoint serta snapshot memungkinkan pemulihan state setelah kegagalan; Flink juga punya konektor untuk Kafka/MSK dan OpenSearch. MSK Connect adalah distraktor terdekat karena bisa mengirim data ke OpenSearch, tetapi konektor sink hanya memindahkan data dan tidak melakukan pemrosesan stateful. Memori Lambda tidak persisten antar invocation sehingga state hilang. Lambda transformasi pada Firehose bersifat stateless per batch. Aturan umum: stream + stateful + fault-tolerant + managed → Managed Service for Apache Flink.","r":["Benar — Flink mendukung keyed state, checkpoint untuk pemulihan, serta konektor MSK dan OpenSearch secara terkelola.","Salah — MSK Connect memindahkan data antar sistem, tetapi tidak menghitung informasi stateful per shipment.","Salah — Memori Lambda tidak tahan lama dan tidak dibagi antar eksekusi, sehingga state bisa hilang.","Salah — Transformasi Lambda di Firehose bersifat stateless per batch, tidak bisa menghitung waktu sejak scan sebelumnya secara andal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'stateful stream processing + exactly-once/checkpoint' → Flink; 'just move data Kafka → sink' → MSK Connect."},{"id":"E1C-45","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"MWAA requirements.txt","q":"After a DAG that uses a new third-party Python library was uploaded to the dags folder of an Amazon MWAA environment, the Airflow UI shows a 'ModuleNotFoundError' import error for the DAG. Which action should the data engineer take to fix the problem?","o":["Add the library with a pinned version to requirements.txt in the environment's S3 bucket, and update the environment to use the new requirements.txt version.","Connect to the MWAA worker hosts through SSH and run pip install.","Copy the library's wheel file into the dags folder next to the DAG.","Increase the environment class to a larger size."],"a":[0],"e":"Error 'ModuleNotFoundError' berarti library Python tidak terinstal di environment. Di MWAA, dependensi Python dikelola melalui file requirements.txt di bucket S3 environment; setelah file diperbarui (sebaiknya dengan versi yang dipin), environment diperbarui agar memakai versi objek requirements.txt yang baru sehingga scheduler dan worker menginstal paket tersebut. Distractor terdekat adalah SSH dan pip install: MWAA adalah layanan terkelola tanpa akses SSH ke host, dan instalasi manual akan hilang saat worker diganti. Menaruh wheel di folder dags tidak membuat paket terinstal. Environment class yang lebih besar tidak menambah library. Aturan umum: dependensi Python MWAA → requirements.txt (dan plugins.zip untuk plugin kustom) di S3.","r":["Benar — requirements.txt di S3 adalah cara resmi menambah paket Python di MWAA.","Salah — Tidak ada akses SSH ke host MWAA dan instalasi manual tidak persisten.","Salah — File di folder dags tidak diinstal sebagai paket Python.","Salah — Ukuran environment tidak terkait dengan modul yang hilang."],"k":"Tips ujian: MWAA ModuleNotFoundError → tambah ke requirements.txt di S3, update environment."},{"id":"E2C-43","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Bedrock knowledge base semantic chunking","q":"A research team ingests long analyst reports into an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. The reports switch topics at irregular points that do not align with page or paragraph sizes, and fixed-size chunks often split a topic in half. The team accepts some additional ingestion cost to improve retrieval accuracy. Which chunking strategy should be used?","o":["Semantic chunking, which uses an embeddings model to split text where the meaning between sentences changes.","Fixed-size chunking with 0% overlap.","No chunking, after manually splitting every report into separate files by topic.","Hierarchical chunking with equal parent and child chunk sizes."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah topik yang berganti 'at irregular points' dan kesediaan menerima 'additional ingestion cost' demi akurasi retrieval. Semantic chunking membagi teks berdasarkan kemiripan makna antar kalimat, dengan parameter seperti maximum tokens, buffer size, dan breakpoint percentile threshold, sehingga batas chunk mengikuti pergantian topik. Strategi ini memakai foundation model sehingga ada biaya tambahan, yang sesuai dengan pernyataan soal. Fixed-size tanpa overlap justru memperburuk pemotongan topik. Memecah file secara manual menambah pekerjaan operasional besar. Hierarchical chunking dengan ukuran parent dan child sama tidak menambah manfaat dan tetap berbasis ukuran token, bukan makna. Aturan umum: batas chunk harus mengikuti makna/topik → semantic chunking (dengan biaya model tambahan).","r":["Benar — Semantic chunking memotong teks pada perubahan makna sehingga topik tidak terpotong di tengah.","Salah — Tanpa overlap, potongan berbasis ukuran makin sering memisahkan topik.","Salah — Pemisahan manual per topik memakan banyak tenaga dan tidak skalabel.","Salah — Hierarchical chunking tetap berbasis ukuran token, dan ukuran parent-child yang sama tidak memberi manfaat."],"k":"Tips ujian: chunk sesuai makna/topik, biaya tambahan diterima → semantic chunking."},{"id":"E1C-33","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions HTTP Task","q":"A serverless ingestion workflow must call a third-party REST API that requires an OAuth client credentials token, and must store the API response for later steps. The team wants to avoid writing and maintaining an AWS Lambda function just to make HTTP calls and wants credentials to be managed securely. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store the client secret in the state machine definition and call the API from a Pass state.","Use an Amazon SQS queue to send requests to the third-party API.","Use a Step Functions HTTP Task that references an Amazon EventBridge connection configured with OAuth authorization.","Use an AWS Glue Python shell job that calls the API with credentials in job parameters."],"a":[2],"e":"Kebutuhannya: panggil 'third-party REST API' dengan OAuth, 'avoid writing ... a Lambda function', dan 'credentials ... managed securely'. Step Functions HTTP Task dapat memanggil endpoint HTTPS publik secara langsung, dengan autentikasi diambil dari EventBridge connection (mendukung Basic, API key, dan OAuth client credentials) yang menyimpan secret di AWS Secrets Manager. Distractor terdekat adalah Glue Python shell job: bisa memanggil API, tetapi menambah kode dan menyimpan kredensial di parameter job, yang tidak aman. Menaruh secret di definisi state machine adalah praktik buruk, dan Pass state tidak melakukan panggilan HTTP. SQS tidak memanggil API eksternal. Aturan umum: panggil API HTTPS dari workflow tanpa Lambda → HTTP Task + EventBridge connection.","r":["Salah — Secret di definisi tidak aman, dan Pass state hanya meneruskan data.","Salah — SQS adalah antrean pesan, bukan klien HTTP ke API eksternal.","Benar — HTTP Task memanggil API langsung, dan EventBridge connection mengelola OAuth dengan secret di Secrets Manager.","Salah — Menambah kode dan menaruh kredensial di parameter job tidak aman."],"k":"Tips ujian: Step Functions memanggil API pihak ketiga tanpa Lambda → HTTP Task + EventBridge connection."},{"id":"E1A-44","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Lambda Kinesis batching window","q":"A Kinesis data stream receives small telemetry records at a steady rate. An AWS Lambda function consumes the stream and is invoked many times per second with only a few records per invocation, which increases cost. A delay of up to 60 seconds is acceptable. What should the data engineer change to reduce the number of invocations?","o":["Register the function as an enhanced fan-out consumer.","Increase the ParallelizationFactor to 10.","Increase the batch size and set MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds on the event source mapping.","Reduce the function timeout to 3 seconds."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'invoked many times per second with only a few records' dan 'delay of up to 60 seconds is acceptable'. Event source mapping Kinesis mendukung batch size (berapa banyak record per invocation) dan MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds (berapa lama Lambda mengumpulkan record sebelum memanggil fungsi, hingga 300 detik). Dengan menaikkan keduanya, setiap invocation memproses lebih banyak record sehingga jumlah invocation dan biaya turun. Distraktor terdekat adalah ParallelizationFactor: justru menambah invocation paralel. Enhanced fan-out mengurangi latensi baca dan memberi throughput khusus, tetapi tidak mengurangi invocation. Mengurangi timeout tidak memengaruhi jumlah invocation. Aturan umum: trade-off batching Lambda = batch lebih besar dan window lebih lama → biaya lebih rendah, latensi lebih tinggi.","r":["Salah — Enhanced fan-out ditujukan untuk throughput dan latensi, bukan mengurangi invocation.","Salah — ParallelizationFactor menambah invocation bersamaan, bukan mengurangi.","Benar — Batch lebih besar dan batching window mengumpulkan lebih banyak record per invocation sehingga invocation berkurang.","Salah — Timeout tidak mengubah jumlah record per invocation."],"k":"Lambda Kinesis terlalu sering dipanggil dengan sedikit record → batch size ↑ + MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds."},{"id":"E1B-44","d":1,"ts":"1.2.6","t":"Writing partitioned output in Glue","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job writes transformed sales data to Amazon S3 as Parquet. Analysts query the data with Amazon Athena and almost always filter by sale date, but every query scans the full dataset. The data engineer wants the job output to support partition pruning by date with the LEAST effort. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write the output as a single large Parquet file per day in the same S3 prefix.","Sort the data by sale date before writing the output.","Convert the output from Parquet to CSV so that Athena can read the date column faster.","Specify partitionKeys such as year, month, and day in the Glue S3 sink so that output is written to Hive-style partition folders, and update the Data Catalog."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah query yang hampir selalu 'filter by sale date' tetapi 'scans the full dataset', dan kebutuhan 'partition pruning'. Dengan partitionKeys pada sink S3 Glue (misalnya year/month/day), output ditulis ke folder bergaya Hive seperti year=2026/month=10/day=14/, dan setelah partisi terdaftar di Data Catalog, Athena hanya memindai folder yang sesuai filter. Menulis satu file per hari dalam prefix yang sama tidak membuat partisi, sehingga Athena tetap memindai semuanya. Mengurutkan data dapat membantu statistik row group Parquet, tetapi tidak memberi partition pruning di tingkat folder. CSV justru menambah data yang dipindai karena tidak kolumnar dan tidak terkompresi efisien. Aturan umum: filter umum di Athena → partisi data menurut kolom tersebut (Hive-style) dan gunakan format kolumnar.","r":["Salah — File dalam prefix yang sama tidak membentuk partisi, sehingga Athena tetap memindai semua data.","Salah — Pengurutan tidak membuat partisi folder sehingga pruning tingkat partisi tidak terjadi.","Salah — CSV memperbesar data yang dipindai dibanding Parquet.","Benar — partitionKeys menghasilkan partisi Hive-style yang dapat dipangkas Athena berdasarkan tanggal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Athena scans everything despite WHERE date' → partition by date (partitionKeys di Glue) + Parquet."},{"id":"E3A-22","d":3,"ts":"3.1.6","t":"DataBrew projects vs recipe jobs","q":"A data engineer built an AWS Glue DataBrew project on a 2 TB dataset in Amazon S3. The interactive session shows only a sample of rows, and the recipe looks correct on the sample. The full dataset must now be cleaned with the same steps every day and written to S3 as Parquet for downstream AWS Glue jobs. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Increase the project sample size until it includes all rows, then export the project view.","Download the sampled result as CSV and upload it to the curated S3 prefix every day.","Rewrite the same transformations as Athena CTAS statements.","Publish the recipe and create a DataBrew recipe job that runs on the full dataset on a daily schedule with Parquet output to S3."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya: sesi project hanya memakai 'sample of rows', sedangkan yang dibutuhkan adalah membersihkan 'full dataset every day' ke 'Parquet'. Di DataBrew, project adalah tempat merancang recipe secara interaktif di atas sampel. Untuk memproses seluruh data, recipe dipublish (diberi versi) lalu dijalankan oleh recipe job terhadap dataset penuh, dengan jadwal harian dan output ke S3 dalam format seperti Parquet. Sampel project memiliki batas ukuran dan tidak dimaksudkan untuk menghasilkan output produksi. Mengunduh hasil sampel jelas tidak mencakup semua data. Menulis ulang sebagai CTAS Athena membuang recipe yang sudah jadi dan menambah kerja. Aturan umum: DataBrew project = desain di sampel; recipe job = eksekusi di data penuh.","r":["Salah — Sampel project dibatasi ukurannya dan bukan mekanisme untuk menghasilkan output produksi.","Salah — Hanya berisi data sampel dan merupakan proses manual.","Salah — Membuang recipe yang sudah ada dan memindahkan logika ke SQL tanpa alasan.","Benar — Recipe job menerapkan recipe yang dipublish ke seluruh dataset sesuai jadwal dengan output Parquet."],"k":"Tips ujian: DataBrew project bekerja di sampel; data penuh diproses oleh recipe job."},{"id":"E4A-22","d":4,"ts":"4.1.6","t":"Managed vs unmanaged shared responsibility","q":"A company is migrating from a self-managed Apache Kafka cluster on Amazon EC2 to Amazon MSK. The security lead asks which security responsibility will remain with the company after the migration. Which responsibility remains with the company?","o":["Patching the operating system of the broker nodes.","Replacing failed broker hardware and maintaining Apache ZooKeeper or KRaft controller nodes.","Configuring client authentication (for example, IAM access control) and granting producers and consumers only the topic permissions they need.","Upgrading the physical network infrastructure in the AWS data center."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'which security responsibility will remain with the company' setelah pindah dari unmanaged ke managed service. Pada layanan managed seperti Amazon MSK, AWS mengelola infrastruktur broker: patching OS, penggantian node yang gagal, dan pengelolaan controller (ZooKeeper atau KRaft). Namun sesuai shared responsibility model, pelanggan tetap bertanggung jawab atas konfigurasi akses data: memilih metode autentikasi klien (IAM access control, SASL/SCRAM, atau mTLS) dan memberi izin topic yang minimal. Pada Kafka self-managed di EC2, semua tugas infrastruktur di atas menjadi tanggung jawab pelanggan. Infrastruktur fisik data center selalu tanggung jawab AWS. Aturan umum: makin managed sebuah service, makin sedikit tanggung jawab infrastruktur Anda, tetapi identitas, permission, dan data tetap tanggung jawab Anda.","r":["Salah — Patching OS broker dikelola AWS di Amazon MSK.","Salah — Penggantian broker dan pengelolaan controller ditangani AWS di MSK.","Benar — Autentikasi klien dan otorisasi per topic tetap tanggung jawab pelanggan di managed service.","Salah — Infrastruktur fisik data center selalu tanggung jawab AWS, baik managed maupun unmanaged."],"k":"Tips ujian: managed service → AWS urus infrastruktur/patching; pelanggan tetap urus IAM, autentikasi klien, dan data."},{"id":"E1B-21","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Spark to Redshift connectivity","q":"A data engineer runs an Apache Spark job on Amazon EMR that reads and writes tables with hundreds of millions of rows in Amazon Redshift. The current implementation uses a generic JDBC connection and writes rows with batched INSERT statements, which takes many hours. Which solution will improve performance the MOST?","o":["Increase the JDBC fetch size and the number of concurrent INSERT connections from each executor.","Replace the JDBC writes with calls to the Redshift Data API for each partition of rows.","Use the Amazon Redshift integration for Apache Spark connector with an Amazon S3 temporary directory so that data is moved with UNLOAD and COPY in parallel.","Export the Spark DataFrame to a single CSV file on the EMR primary node and load it with a single INSERT statement."],"a":[2],"e":"Masalah utamanya adalah transfer data dalam jumlah sangat besar antara Spark dan Redshift melalui JDBC dan INSERT yang lambat. Konektor Amazon Redshift integration for Apache Spark memakai S3 sebagai staging perantara: pembacaan memakai UNLOAD paralel dan penulisan memakai COPY paralel, yang merupakan cara paling efisien untuk memindahkan data massal ke dan dari Redshift. Menaikkan fetch size dan koneksi INSERT adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi INSERT tetap jauh lebih lambat daripada COPY dan bisa membebani leader node. Redshift Data API dirancang untuk menjalankan statement SQL secara asinkron, bukan transfer massal. Menulis satu file CSV di primary node menciptakan bottleneck dan INSERT tunggal tidak memuat file. Aturan umum: data massal ke Redshift → COPY dari S3, dan dari Redshift → UNLOAD ke S3.","r":["Salah — Tuning JDBC membantu sedikit, tetapi INSERT batch tetap jauh lebih lambat daripada COPY paralel.","Salah — Data API untuk menjalankan SQL asinkron, bukan untuk memindahkan ratusan juta baris.","Benar — Konektor memakai staging S3 dengan UNLOAD/COPY paralel, cara tercepat untuk data massal.","Salah — Satu file di primary node menjadi bottleneck dan INSERT tunggal tidak dapat memuat file."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'bulk load into Redshift' → COPY dari S3 (staging); hindari INSERT baris per baris."},{"id":"E3B-06","d":3,"ts":"3.3.1","t":"Redshift audit logging","q":"A financial company uses an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster. Auditors require a durable record of every SQL statement run against the cluster, including the user and the query text, retained outside the cluster for 1 year. Which TWO actions must a data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Turn on Redshift audit logging with Amazon S3 or CloudWatch Logs as the destination.","Set the enable_user_activity_logging parameter to true in the cluster's parameter group.","Create a CloudTrail trail with data events enabled for Amazon Redshift to capture SQL text from JDBC clients.","Query the STL_QUERY system table once per year and export the results.","Enable Redshift enhanced VPC routing."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Persyaratannya adalah 'every SQL statement' dengan 'query text' yang disimpan 'outside the cluster for 1 year'. Redshift audit logging menghasilkan connection log, user log, dan user activity log ke S3 atau CloudWatch Logs. Namun user activity log (yang berisi teks setiap query) hanya tercatat jika parameter enable_user_activity_logging diset true di parameter group — tanpa itu hanya connection dan user log yang tersedia. CloudTrail hanya mencatat panggilan API Redshift (seperti CreateCluster), bukan teks SQL dari klien JDBC/ODBC. Tabel sistem STL hanya menyimpan beberapa hari riwayat sehingga ekspor tahunan akan kehilangan data. Ingat: audit SQL Redshift = audit logging + enable_user_activity_logging.","r":["Benar — Audit logging mengirim log koneksi, user, dan aktivitas ke S3 atau CloudWatch Logs di luar cluster.","Benar — Parameter ini wajib agar user activity log yang berisi teks setiap query ikut tercatat.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API manajemen Redshift, bukan teks SQL yang dijalankan lewat JDBC.","Salah — Tabel STL hanya menyimpan riwayat beberapa hari, jadi ekspor tahunan tidak lengkap.","Salah — Enhanced VPC routing mengatur jalur traffic COPY/UNLOAD, bukan logging query."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift 'log every query' → audit logging + enable_user_activity_logging = true."},{"id":"E4B-09","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"EMR security configuration","q":"A company runs Apache Spark jobs on Amazon EMR on EC2. Security requirements state that data in Amazon S3 accessed through EMRFS must be encrypted with SSE-KMS, data on local disks of cluster nodes (including HDFS and EBS volumes) must be encrypted with an AWS KMS key, and data exchanged between cluster nodes must be encrypted in transit. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Enable default SSE-KMS encryption on the S3 buckets and enable EBS encryption by default for the account.","Write a bootstrap action that configures LUKS on every node and configures TLS for each application.","Register the S3 locations with AWS Lake Formation and enable Lake Formation encryption.","Create an Amazon EMR security configuration that enables at-rest encryption for EMRFS with SSE-KMS, local disk encryption with a KMS key, and in-transit encryption with TLS certificates, and specify it when launching the cluster."],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhan mencakup tiga lapisan: EMRFS di S3, 'local disks ... including HDFS and EBS volumes', dan 'between cluster nodes ... in transit', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. EMR security configuration adalah fitur bawaan yang dapat mengaktifkan at-rest encryption untuk EMRFS (SSE-S3, SSE-KMS, atau CSE-KMS), local disk encryption memakai KMS key (termasuk volume EBS dan instance store), serta in-transit encryption dengan sertifikat TLS, lalu dipakai ulang saat membuat cluster. Distraktor terdekat adalah default encryption S3 + EBS by default: menutup sebagian at rest, tetapi tidak mencakup in-transit antar node dan tidak menangani instance store. Bootstrap action LUKS/TLS kustom bisa berhasil namun overhead-nya tinggi dan rawan kesalahan. Lake Formation tidak menyediakan pengaturan enkripsi disk/transit EMR. Aturan umum: enkripsi EMR at rest + in transit → EMR security configuration.","r":["Salah — Tidak mencakup enkripsi in-transit antar node dan tidak menangani instance store lokal.","Salah — Skrip bootstrap kustom bisa bekerja tetapi menambah overhead operasional dan risiko kesalahan.","Salah — Lake Formation mengelola izin akses data, bukan enkripsi disk lokal atau trafik antar node EMR.","Benar — EMR security configuration menangani EMRFS SSE-KMS, local disk encryption, dan TLS in transit secara terpusat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'EMR encryption at rest (EMRFS + local disk) and in transit' → EMR security configuration."},{"id":"E4A-34","d":4,"ts":"4.2.2","t":"Parameter Store vs Secrets Manager","q":"A data pipeline running on Amazon ECS needs about 40 configuration values (such as bucket names and API endpoints) and one database password. The password does not need automatic rotation. The company wants to store all values centrally, encrypt the password, and minimize cost. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Store all values, including the configuration values, as secrets in AWS Secrets Manager.","Store the configuration values and the password as plaintext environment variables in the ECS task definition.","Store all values in a JSON file in Amazon S3 with SSE-S3 encryption and read the file at startup.","Store the configuration values as AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store String parameters and the password as a SecureString parameter in the standard tier."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'does not need automatic rotation', 'encrypt the password', dan 'minimize cost'. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store tier standar tidak dikenakan biaya penyimpanan, mendukung parameter String untuk konfigurasi dan SecureString yang dienkripsi dengan AWS KMS untuk password. ECS juga dapat menyuntikkan parameter ini ke container secara native. Secrets Manager dikenakan biaya per secret per bulan; untuk 41 nilai tanpa kebutuhan rotasi, biaya itu tidak perlu. Plaintext environment variable tidak mengenkripsi password. File JSON di S3 berfungsi, tetapi bukan penyimpanan konfigurasi terpusat dengan kontrol akses per parameter dan riwayat versi. Aturan umum: konfigurasi + secret tanpa rotasi, biaya rendah → Parameter Store (SecureString); butuh rotasi otomatis → Secrets Manager.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi biaya per secret untuk 41 nilai tanpa kebutuhan rotasi tidak hemat.","Salah — Password disimpan tanpa enkripsi di task definition.","Salah — Tidak memberi kontrol akses per nilai dan bukan layanan konfigurasi terpusat yang dirancang untuk ini.","Benar — Parameter Store standard tier gratis, String untuk konfigurasi dan SecureString terenkripsi KMS untuk password."],"k":"Tips ujian: secret tanpa rotasi + biaya minimal → Parameter Store SecureString; rotasi otomatis → Secrets Manager."},{"id":"E3B-46","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"Data remediation with DataBrew recipes","q":"A customer address dataset is refreshed nightly. Downstream reports break when the country field is empty or contains free text such as 'indonesia ' or 'ID.'. Business analysts with no coding experience must remediate the data every night by trimming whitespace, standardizing values to ISO country codes, and filling missing values with 'UNKNOWN'. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Write a PySpark script and run it on a persistent Amazon EMR cluster.","Ask the source system owners to fix the data before every nightly load.","Build an AWS Glue DataBrew recipe with steps to trim, replace values, and fill missing values, and run it as a scheduled DataBrew recipe job.","Create an Amazon Athena view that uses CASE expressions for all known spellings."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'business analysts with no coding experience', remediasi berupa 'trimming whitespace', 'standardizing values', 'filling missing values', serta 'every night'. AWS Glue DataBrew menyediakan lebih dari 250 transformasi visual, termasuk trim, replace value/mapping, dan fill missing values, yang disimpan sebagai recipe dan dijalankan otomatis sebagai recipe job terjadwal. Distraktor terdekat adalah view Athena dengan CASE: butuh SQL, tidak menulis data yang sudah diperbaiki, dan harus diperbarui setiap ada ejaan baru. Script PySpark di EMR persisten melanggar syarat tanpa kode dan menambah overhead. Meminta sumber memperbaiki tidak dapat diandalkan. Aturan: validasi + remediasi tanpa kode yang berulang → DataBrew recipe job terjadwal.","r":["Salah — Butuh kemampuan coding dan mengelola cluster persisten.","Salah — Tidak ada jaminan sumber akan memperbaiki data setiap malam.","Benar — DataBrew recipe visual dengan job terjadwal memungkinkan analis non-coder meremediasi data secara rutin.","Salah — View SQL perlu dirawat manual untuk setiap variasi dan butuh kemampuan SQL."],"k":"Tips ujian: no-code data cleaning/remediation terjadwal → DataBrew recipe job."},{"id":"E1B-64","d":1,"ts":"1.2.9","t":"Volume and velocity architecture","q":"A manufacturing company has 50,000 IoT sensors that each send a 1 KB reading every 0.25 seconds (about 200,000 events per second). Operations dashboards must show aggregated metrics within 10 seconds, and all raw readings must be retained for 1 year for low-cost batch analytics. Which TWO components should be part of the solution? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Write each reading directly into an Amazon RDS for MySQL table.","Amazon Kinesis Data Streams with Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink to compute the real-time aggregates for the dashboards.","Store the raw readings in Amazon DynamoDB for 1 year and run full table scans for analytics.","Amazon Data Firehose to deliver the raw readings to Amazon S3 in Parquet format for long-term analytics.","Send the readings to an Amazon SQS FIFO queue and process them with a single consumer."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Ada dua kebutuhan yang dipicu oleh karakteristik data: velocity tinggi ('about 200,000 events per second') dengan dashboard 'within 10 seconds', dan volume besar yang harus disimpan '1 year for low-cost batch analytics'. Kinesis Data Streams dengan Managed Service for Apache Flink menangani throughput tinggi dan menghitung agregat secara real time. Firehose mengirim data mentah ke S3 dalam format Parquet, yang murah untuk disimpan lama dan efisien untuk analitik batch dengan Athena atau Glue. RDS MySQL tidak dirancang untuk 200 ribu insert per detik dan mahal untuk penyimpanan jangka panjang. DynamoDB dengan full table scan untuk analitik mahal dan lambat. SQS FIFO memiliki batas throughput dan satu konsumen tidak bisa mengimbangi laju ini. Aturan umum: pisahkan jalur hot (streaming real-time) dan cold (S3 data lake kolumnar) sesuai velocity dan volume.","r":["Salah — Insert per event ke RDS pada 200 ribu event/detik tidak skalabel dan mahal untuk retensi panjang.","Benar — KDS + Flink menangani velocity tinggi dan agregasi real-time dalam hitungan detik.","Salah — Full scan DynamoDB untuk analitik mahal dan tidak efisien.","Benar — Firehose ke S3 Parquet menyediakan penyimpanan jangka panjang yang murah untuk analitik batch.","Salah — Throughput SQS FIFO terbatas dan satu konsumen tidak mampu mengimbangi beban."],"k":"Tips ujian: high velocity + long retention → hot path KDS/Flink + cold path Firehose → S3 (Parquet)."},{"id":"E3A-33","d":3,"ts":"3.1.9","t":"EventBridge S3 event rules","q":"A data engineer wants an AWS Step Functions workflow to start automatically whenever a new object is written to the incoming/ prefix of an Amazon S3 bucket, but not for objects written to other prefixes. The solution should use event filtering without custom code. Which steps should the data engineer take?","o":["Configure an S3 event notification that sends events to an Amazon SQS queue and poll the queue from an Amazon EC2 instance that starts the workflow.","Create an AWS CloudTrail trail for S3 data events and query it every minute with Amazon Athena to find new objects.","Schedule the workflow every minute and have the first state list new objects under incoming/.","Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the bucket and create an EventBridge rule with an event pattern for Object Created events with the incoming/ key prefix, targeting the state machine."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'start automatically whenever a new object is written', 'only the incoming/ prefix', dan 'without custom code'. Bucket S3 bisa mengirim semua event ke Amazon EventBridge setelah opsi notifikasi EventBridge diaktifkan. Rule EventBridge dengan event pattern (source aws.s3, detail-type Object Created, nama bucket, dan filter prefix pada object key) memfilter event secara deklaratif, lalu menjalankan state machine Step Functions sebagai target. Polling SQS dari EC2 menambah server dan kode. CloudTrail + Athena tiap menit lambat dan mahal. Menjadwalkan workflow setiap menit membuang eksekusi dan membutuhkan logika listing. Aturan umum: pipeline berbasis event dari S3 dengan filter → aktifkan EventBridge di bucket + rule dengan event pattern.","r":["Salah — Membutuhkan instance EC2 dan kode polling, sehingga overhead lebih besar.","Salah — Pendekatan lambat dan mahal untuk sekadar mendeteksi objek baru.","Salah — Polling terjadwal membuang eksekusi dan butuh kode untuk menemukan objek baru.","Benar — Rule EventBridge memfilter Object Created berdasarkan prefix dan langsung memulai state machine."],"k":"Tips ujian: S3 event → Step Functions dengan filter prefix → aktifkan 'Amazon EventBridge' di bucket + rule event pattern."},{"id":"E3B-68","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"Kinesis hot shard and partition key skew","q":"An IoT platform writes records to an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream with 20 shards, using device_type as the partition key. There are only three device types, and one type sends 80% of the traffic. Producers receive ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors for one shard while most shards are idle. Which solution will resolve the issue MOST effectively?","o":["Double the number of shards in the stream.","Use a high-cardinality partition key such as device_id so that records are distributed across all shards.","Enable enhanced fan-out for the consumers.","Increase the stream's data retention period to 7 days."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejala kuncinya: 'only three device types' sebagai partition key, satu shard terkena throttling sementara 'most shards are idle'. Kinesis memetakan partition key ke shard melalui hash, sehingga semua record dengan device_type yang sama selalu masuk ke shard yang sama (hot shard). Menggunakan kunci berkardinalitas tinggi seperti device_id menyebarkan record ke seluruh shard. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah shard: dengan hanya tiga kunci, paling banyak tiga shard yang terpakai dan kunci dominan tetap di satu shard, sehingga throttling berlanjut. Enhanced fan-out meningkatkan throughput baca konsumen, bukan tulis. Retensi tidak memengaruhi throughput. Aturan: hot shard → partition key berkardinalitas tinggi (atau tambahkan suffix acak).","r":["Salah — Kunci yang sama tetap di-hash ke satu shard, jadi shard tambahan tetap idle.","Benar — Kunci berkardinalitas tinggi menyebarkan beban tulis ke semua shard.","Salah — Enhanced fan-out menambah throughput baca untuk konsumen, bukan kapasitas tulis per shard.","Salah — Retensi data tidak memengaruhi batas throughput shard."],"k":"Tips ujian: satu shard throttled, shard lain idle → ganti partition key ke high-cardinality."},{"id":"E4A-10","d":4,"ts":"4.1.3","t":"Secrets Manager rotation strategies","q":"A company rotates the password of an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL user every 7 days by using AWS Secrets Manager with the single user rotation strategy. Long-running ETL jobs sometimes fail with authentication errors when they open new connections in the short window during which the password is being changed. The company needs rotation to continue without these failures. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Increase the rotation interval to 90 days so that failures happen less often.","Switch to storing the password in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and rotate it manually during maintenance windows.","Configure the ETL jobs to always read the AWSPREVIOUS version of the secret.","Switch the rotation strategy to alternating users so that Secrets Manager alternates between two database users that each always have a valid password."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'without these failures' saat jendela rotasi. Pada strategi single user, password user yang sama diubah di database, sehingga ada jeda singkat ketika password lama sudah tidak berlaku tetapi klien belum mengambil versi baru. Strategi alternating users memakai dua user database (misalnya app_user dan app_user_clone): setiap rotasi memperbarui password user yang sedang tidak aktif, lalu label AWSCURRENT dipindahkan, sehingga credential yang sedang dipakai klien tetap valid. Memperpanjang interval hanya mengurangi frekuensi masalah dan bisa melanggar kebijakan rotasi. Rotasi manual di Parameter Store menambah overhead. AWSPREVIOUS berarti selalu memakai password lama yang suatu saat tidak valid. Aturan umum: butuh high availability saat rotasi → alternating users strategy.","r":["Salah — Masalah tetap ada, hanya lebih jarang, dan interval 90 hari bisa melanggar kebijakan keamanan.","Salah — Rotasi manual menambah overhead dan tetap menyebabkan jeda saat password diganti.","Salah — Versi AWSPREVIOUS adalah password lama yang tidak lagi berlaku setelah rotasi pada single user.","Benar — Alternating users menjaga selalu ada satu credential valid sehingga koneksi baru tidak gagal saat rotasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: rotasi menyebabkan gagal login sesaat → alternating users rotation strategy."},{"id":"E4A-45","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation row-level data filters","q":"A global retail company stores order data in an AWS Glue Data Catalog table that is governed by AWS Lake Formation and queried with Amazon Athena. Analysts in the Indonesia office must see only rows where country = 'ID', and analysts in the Singapore office must see only rows where country = 'SG'. All columns can be shown. The company does not want to create copies of the data or separate views. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create Lake Formation data filters with the row filter expressions country = 'ID' and country = 'SG', and grant SELECT on the table through the matching data filter to each office's IAM role.","Partition the table by country and grant each office's IAM role s3:GetObject on its country prefix.","Create two Athena workgroups and configure each workgroup with a default WHERE clause on country.","Use AWS Glue jobs to write separate tables for each country and grant access to each table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'see only rows where country = ...' tanpa 'copies of the data or separate views'. Lake Formation data filter mendukung row-level security melalui row filter expression; grant SELECT melalui data filter membuat Athena (dan engine terintegrasi lain) hanya mengembalikan baris yang memenuhi ekspresi. Filter ditegakkan oleh Lake Formation, sehingga analis tidak dapat menghindarinya dengan menulis query sendiri. Izin S3 per prefix partition melewati Lake Formation dan bisa diakali dengan akses langsung ke tabel penuh. Athena workgroup tidak mempunyai fitur 'default WHERE clause'. Tabel per negara menggandakan data. Aturan umum: row-level security di data lake → Lake Formation data filter dengan row filter expression.","r":["Benar — Data filter dengan row filter expression membatasi baris per kantor tanpa duplikasi.","Salah — Akses S3 langsung tidak dikelola Lake Formation dan bukan kontrol row-level yang andal.","Salah — Workgroup tidak menyediakan filter baris otomatis.","Salah — Membuat salinan data per negara melanggar syarat dan menambah overhead."],"k":"Tips ujian: row-level security di Athena/data lake → Lake Formation data filter (row filter expression)."},{"id":"E3B-10","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"EventBridge with CloudTrail API events","q":"A data engineer must notify the security team in near real time whenever someone calls glue:DeleteDatabase or s3:PutBucketPolicy in the data lake account. A CloudTrail trail is already enabled. The solution must have the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events for those event names and targets an Amazon SNS topic.","Schedule an AWS Lambda function every 15 minutes that calls the CloudTrail LookupEvents API and publishes matches to Amazon SNS.","Create an S3 event notification on the trail bucket that invokes a Lambda function to parse every log file.","Run a daily Amazon Athena query over the trail logs and email the results."],"a":[0],"e":"Persyaratannya 'near real time' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. CloudTrail mengirim event panggilan API ke EventBridge sebagai detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', sehingga rule EventBridge dengan pola eventSource dan eventName tertentu bisa langsung menarget SNS tanpa kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah S3 event notification plus Lambda parsing file log, yang bekerja tetapi lebih lambat (file log dikirim per beberapa menit) dan butuh kode parsing. Polling LookupEvents setiap 15 menit dan query Athena harian tidak near real time. Aturan: reaksi otomatis terhadap panggilan API tertentu → EventBridge rule pada event CloudTrail.","r":["Benar — EventBridge menerima event API dari CloudTrail dan rule pola eventName dapat langsung mengirim ke SNS tanpa kode.","Salah — Polling Lambda menambah kode dan delay hingga 15 menit.","Salah — Parsing setiap file log dengan Lambda menambah kode dan latensi pengiriman file log.","Salah — Query harian jauh dari near real time."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'alert when specific API is called' → EventBridge rule (AWS API Call via CloudTrail) → SNS."},{"id":"E1B-66","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Bedrock Data Automation","q":"A logistics company receives thousands of invoices and delivery receipts each day as PDFs and photos in Amazon S3. The layouts differ by vendor. The company needs to extract specific fields such as invoice number, vendor name, line items, and total amount into structured JSON for loading into the data lake. The company wants to use generative AI with the LEAST custom development. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Write AWS Glue jobs with regular expressions for each vendor's layout.","Use Amazon Bedrock Data Automation with a custom blueprint that defines the fields to extract, and process the documents from Amazon S3.","Train a custom document-understanding model from scratch with Amazon SageMaker AI.","Use Amazon Comprehend sentiment analysis on the raw document files."],"a":[1],"e":"Penentunya adalah dokumen tidak terstruktur (PDF dan foto) dengan 'layouts differ by vendor', kebutuhan field spesifik dalam 'structured JSON', serta generative AI dengan 'LEAST custom development'. Amazon Bedrock Data Automation memakai foundation model untuk mengekstrak informasi dari dokumen, gambar, audio, dan video menjadi output terstruktur, dan blueprint kustom memungkinkan Anda menentukan field yang diinginkan tanpa membangun model. Regex per vendor di Glue rapuh terhadap variasi layout dan tidak bisa membaca foto tanpa OCR. Melatih model dari nol di SageMaker AI membutuhkan data berlabel dan usaha ML yang besar. Sentiment analysis tidak mengekstrak field. Aturan umum: ekstraksi terstruktur dari konten tidak terstruktur dengan GenAI → Bedrock Data Automation.","r":["Salah — Regex per layout rapuh, mahal dipelihara, dan tidak menangani gambar.","Benar — Bedrock Data Automation dengan blueprint mengekstrak field yang ditentukan ke JSON tanpa membangun model.","Salah — Melatih model dari nol membutuhkan data berlabel dan pengembangan ML yang besar.","Salah — Analisis sentimen tidak mengekstrak field seperti nomor faktur atau total."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'extract structured fields from documents/images/audio/video with GenAI, least effort' → Amazon Bedrock Data Automation."},{"id":"E1C-22","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Step Functions Catch and compensation","q":"In an AWS Step Functions workflow, an AWS Glue job writes partial output to Amazon S3 before it fails. When this happens, the workflow must delete the partial output, notify the on-call team with the original input and the error details, and the execution must still be recorded as failed. Which design meets these requirements?","o":["Add a Retry on the Glue task with MaxAttempts 3 and no other error handling.","Add a Catch on the Glue task with ResultPath set to $.error that goes to a cleanup Lambda task, then to an Amazon SNS Publish task, and then to a Fail state.","Add a Catch on the Glue task that goes to the SNS Publish task and then to a Succeed state.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for failed executions that invokes a Lambda function to delete the S3 output."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhan: 'delete the partial output', notifikasi berisi 'original input and the error details', dan eksekusi 'still recorded as failed'. Catch dengan ResultPath '$.error' menambahkan info error ke input asli (bukan menimpanya), lalu alur menjalankan cleanup Lambda, publish SNS dengan konteks lengkap, dan diakhiri Fail state sehingga status eksekusi tetap FAILED untuk monitoring. Distractor terdekat adalah Catch yang berakhir di Succeed state: cleanup dan notifikasi terjadi, tetapi eksekusi tercatat sukses sehingga metrik ExecutionsFailed dan alarm tidak menangkap masalah. Retry saja tidak membersihkan output parsial. Rule EventBridge bisa membersihkan, tetapi memecah logika ke luar workflow dan tidak memenuhi notifikasi dengan konteks error secara terstruktur. Aturan umum: Catch + ResultPath untuk mempertahankan input, langkah kompensasi, lalu Fail state.","r":["Salah — Retry tidak menghapus output parsial atau memberi notifikasi.","Benar — Catch dengan ResultPath mempertahankan input dan error, menjalankan cleanup dan notifikasi, lalu Fail state menjaga status gagal.","Salah — Berakhir di Succeed menyembunyikan kegagalan dari monitoring.","Salah — Logika kompensasi terpecah di luar workflow dan notifikasi tim tidak tercakup."],"k":"Tips ujian: Catch → cleanup → notify → Fail state; ResultPath '$.error' menjaga input asli."},{"id":"E4B-33","d":4,"ts":"4.4.4","t":"Log analytics with OpenSearch Service","q":"An operations team collects application logs from hundreds of microservices into Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The team needs near-real-time full-text search with relevance ranking across all services, rich interactive dashboards that correlate events, and the ability to keep 30 days of logs searchable. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Export the logs to Amazon S3 every day and query them with Amazon Athena.","Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to run saved queries on each log group.","Use CloudWatch Logs subscription filters to stream the logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service and use OpenSearch Dashboards for search and visualization.","Load the logs into Amazon Redshift every hour and build reports in Amazon Quick."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'near-real-time full-text search with relevance ranking' dan 'rich interactive dashboards that correlate events'. Amazon OpenSearch Service adalah mesin pencarian dan analitik log yang mendukung full-text search berbasis indeks terbalik dengan relevance scoring, dan OpenSearch Dashboards menyediakan visualisasi interaktif untuk korelasi log. Subscription filter mengalirkan log dari CloudWatch Logs ke OpenSearch hampir real-time, dan index lifecycle dapat menghapus data setelah 30 hari. Distraktor terdekat adalah CloudWatch Logs Insights: bagus untuk query ad hoc, tetapi tidak menyediakan relevance ranking full-text dan dashboard korelasi sekaya OpenSearch. Export harian ke S3 + Athena tidak near-real-time. Redshift + Quick cocok untuk analitik terstruktur, bukan pencarian teks log real-time. Aturan umum: log search + dashboard real-time → OpenSearch Service; ad hoc → Logs Insights; batch/murah atas S3 → Athena.","r":["Salah — Export harian tidak near-real-time dan Athena tidak menyediakan relevance ranking full-text.","Salah — Logs Insights cocok untuk query ad hoc, bukan pencarian full-text dengan relevance ranking dan dashboard korelasi kaya.","Benar — OpenSearch Service menyediakan full-text search hampir real-time dan dashboard interaktif.","Salah — Load per jam ke Redshift tidak near-real-time dan tidak dirancang untuk pencarian teks log."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'full-text search + real-time log dashboards' → Amazon OpenSearch Service."},{"id":"E3B-21","d":3,"ts":"3.3.3","t":"CloudWatch anomaly detection alarms","q":"An Amazon Data Firehose stream ingests clickstream data. Its IncomingRecords metric follows a strong daily pattern: high during business hours and close to zero overnight. The team wants to be alerted when ingestion drops unexpectedly at any time of day, but static thresholds either fire every night or miss daytime drops. Which solution meets this requirement with the LEAST effort?","o":["Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses anomaly detection on the IncomingRecords metric and alerts when the value is below the expected band.","Create two static alarms, one for business hours and one for nights, and enable and disable them with a scheduled Lambda function.","Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter on the Firehose error log group.","Enable CloudTrail Insights on the account."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'strong daily pattern' dan masalah 'static thresholds'. CloudWatch anomaly detection melatih model dari data historis metrik (termasuk pola harian/mingguan) dan membentuk band nilai yang diharapkan; alarm dapat dipicu saat metrik berada di bawah band (LessThanLowerThreshold). Ini menangani pola musiman tanpa threshold manual. Distraktor terdekat adalah dua alarm statis yang diaktifkan bergantian lewat Lambda — rumit, butuh kode, dan tetap kasar. Metric filter pada error log tidak mendeteksi turunnya volume. CloudTrail Insights menganalisis panggilan API, bukan metrik data. Aturan: metrik dengan pola musiman → anomaly detection alarm.","r":["Benar — Anomaly detection mempelajari pola harian dan memicu alarm saat nilai berada di bawah band yang diharapkan.","Salah — Menambah kode penjadwalan dan threshold statis tetap tidak akurat.","Salah — Error log tidak mencerminkan penurunan volume data yang masuk.","Salah — Insights menganalisis volume panggilan API, bukan metrik ingestion."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'seasonal/daily pattern' + 'no static threshold' → CloudWatch anomaly detection alarm."},{"id":"E2A-44","d":2,"ts":"2.1.5","t":"Redshift federated query setup","q":"A data engineer is setting up Amazon Redshift federated queries so that the Redshift cluster can query an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database in the same VPC. Which TWO steps are required? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Store the database credentials in AWS Secrets Manager and run CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA ... FROM POSTGRES that references the secret ARN and an IAM role allowed to read the secret.","Run an AWS Glue crawler on the RDS database to create tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog.","Configure the RDS security group to allow inbound traffic on the PostgreSQL port from the Redshift cluster's security group or subnets.","Unload the RDS tables to Amazon S3 in Parquet format before running queries.","Enable Amazon RDS Performance Insights on the source database."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah langkah yang 'required' agar Redshift dapat melakukan federated query ke RDS PostgreSQL. Pertama, Redshift memerlukan external schema yang dibuat dengan CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA ... FROM POSTGRES, yang mereferensikan secret di AWS Secrets Manager berisi kredensial database serta IAM role yang diberi izin membaca secret tersebut. Kedua, harus ada konektivitas jaringan: security group RDS harus mengizinkan koneksi masuk pada port PostgreSQL dari Redshift. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue crawler: crawler dipakai untuk Spectrum/Athena atas data katalog, tetapi federated query membaca metadata langsung dari database sumber. Unload ke S3 justru mengubahnya menjadi pola Spectrum, bukan federated. Performance Insights hanya untuk pemantauan. Aturan umum: federated query = external schema + Secrets Manager + IAM role + konektivitas jaringan.","r":["Benar — External schema federated memerlukan referensi ke secret kredensial di Secrets Manager dan IAM role yang dapat membacanya.","Salah — Federated query tidak memakai Glue Data Catalog; metadata dibaca langsung dari database PostgreSQL.","Benar — Tanpa aturan security group yang mengizinkan koneksi dari Redshift, query federated tidak dapat menjangkau RDS.","Salah — Unload ke S3 bukan bagian dari federated query dan menghilangkan manfaat akses data live.","Salah — Performance Insights adalah fitur pemantauan, bukan prasyarat federated query."],"k":"Federated query setup → CREATE EXTERNAL SCHEMA FROM POSTGRES/MYSQL + Secrets Manager + IAM role + network access."},{"id":"E2C-48","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Bedrock knowledge base data source sync","q":"Every night, an AWS Glue job writes new and updated product manuals to the Amazon S3 data source of an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base. Users report that answers do not include content from documents uploaded in the last week. The data engineer confirms that the files are in the correct S3 prefix. What should the data engineer do to keep the knowledge base current with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Delete and recreate the knowledge base every night.","After the Glue job finishes, start an ingestion job (data source sync) on the knowledge base, for example from an AWS Step Functions workflow.","Increase the number of results returned by the Retrieve API.","Move the documents into the prompt of every request instead of using the knowledge base."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah dokumen baru sudah ada di S3 tetapi tidak muncul di jawaban, serta 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon Bedrock knowledge base tidak otomatis memproses file baru di data source S3; perubahan baru masuk ke vector store setelah ingestion job (sync) dijalankan, misalnya dengan API StartIngestionJob. Sync bersifat incremental, hanya memproses dokumen yang ditambahkan, diubah, atau dihapus. Memicu sync dari workflow orkestrasi setelah job Glue selesai membuat proses otomatis. Menghapus dan membuat ulang knowledge base setiap malam memboroskan biaya embedding dan berisiko downtime. Menaikkan jumlah hasil tidak membantu karena vektor dokumen baru belum ada. Memasukkan dokumen ke prompt melampaui batas konteks dan mahal. Aturan umum: data source berubah → jalankan ingestion job/sync (incremental).","r":["Salah — Membuat ulang knowledge base setiap malam memproses ulang semua dokumen dan menambah biaya.","Benar — Ingestion job incremental setelah job Glue membuat vector store mengikuti dokumen terbaru secara otomatis.","Salah — Vektor dokumen baru belum ada, jadi menambah jumlah hasil tidak membantu.","Salah — Memasukkan seluruh dokumen ke prompt mahal dan melampaui batas konteks."],"k":"Tips ujian: dokumen baru di S3 belum muncul di knowledge base → jalankan sync/ingestion job."},{"id":"E4B-56","d":4,"ts":"4.5.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog fine-grained subscription","q":"In Amazon SageMaker Catalog, the Finance project publishes an AWS Glue table containing transactions for all regions, including a salary_band column. A subscription request arrives from the EU Analytics project. Company policy states that this project may see only rows where region = 'EU' and must not see the salary_band column. The data owner wants to avoid creating and maintaining a separate copy of the table. What should the data owner do?","o":["Approve the subscription request by using 'Approve with row and column filters', selecting a row filter for region = 'EU' and a column filter that excludes salary_band.","Create a new filtered table with an AWS Glue job, publish it as a separate asset, and approve subscriptions only to that asset.","Approve the request with full access and ask the EU Analytics team to filter the data in their queries.","Apply Amazon Redshift dynamic data masking to the salary_band column."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: hanya 'rows where region = EU', tanpa kolom 'salary_band', dan 'avoid creating and maintaining a separate copy'. SageMaker Catalog mendukung fine-grained access control saat approval: pemilik dapat memilih 'Approve with row and column filters'. Untuk tabel AWS Glue, filter-filter tersebut digabungkan menjadi satu Lake Formation data cell filter, dan project subscriber menerima izin SELECT read-only melalui filter itu (untuk Redshift, dibuat late-binding view yang dibatasi). Distraktor terdekat adalah membuat tabel terfilter dengan Glue job: hasilnya benar, tetapi menciptakan salinan yang harus dipelihara, melanggar syarat. Full access dengan permintaan untuk memfilter sendiri bukan kontrol keamanan. Redshift dynamic data masking tidak berlaku untuk tabel Glue dan tidak memfilter baris. Aturan umum: subscription dengan pembatasan baris/kolom di SageMaker Catalog → approve with row and column filters (Lake Formation data cell filter).","r":["Benar — Row dan column filter saat approval diterapkan sebagai Lake Formation data cell filter tanpa salinan data.","Salah — Membuat salinan terfilter menambah duplikasi dan beban pemeliharaan.","Salah — Full access mengekspos data terlarang; filter di sisi consumer bukan kontrol keamanan.","Salah — DDM Redshift tidak berlaku untuk tabel Glue dan tidak membatasi baris."],"k":"Tips ujian: SageMaker Catalog + 'only some rows/columns' → Approve with row and column filters → LF data cell filter."},{"id":"E1B-55","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"Creating data APIs with API Gateway","q":"A company stores customer loyalty profiles in an Amazon DynamoDB table. A partner's mobile application must retrieve a single customer's profile by customer ID through an HTTPS REST endpoint with low latency. The company wants a fully managed, serverless solution with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Deploy a REST service on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer that queries DynamoDB.","Export the DynamoDB table to Amazon S3 every hour and let the partner query it with Amazon Athena.","Create an Amazon API Gateway REST API with a resource that invokes an AWS Lambda function to read the item from DynamoDB.","Load the DynamoDB data into Amazon Redshift and give the partner JDBC access."],"a":[2],"e":"Penentunya adalah 'HTTPS REST endpoint', pembacaan item tunggal 'by customer ID' dengan 'low latency', serta 'fully managed, serverless' dengan overhead terendah. API Gateway menyediakan endpoint REST terkelola (dengan autentikasi, throttling, dan monitoring), dan Lambda membaca item dari DynamoDB dengan GetItem dalam milidetik; keduanya serverless. EC2 di belakang ALB adalah distraktor yang bisa bekerja, tetapi Anda harus mengelola server, patch, dan scaling. Export ke S3 + Athena tidak menyediakan endpoint REST dan latensinya detik serta datanya tertinggal. Redshift dengan JDBC bukan API untuk aplikasi mobile dan tidak cocok untuk lookup per item berlatensi rendah. Aturan umum: membuat data API serverless → API Gateway + Lambda (atau integrasi langsung) ke DynamoDB/sumber data.","r":["Salah — Mengelola EC2 dan ALB menambah overhead operasional.","Salah — Bukan endpoint REST, latensinya tinggi, dan data tidak terkini.","Benar — API Gateway + Lambda + DynamoDB adalah API serverless berlatensi rendah dengan overhead minimal.","Salah — JDBC ke Redshift tidak sesuai untuk aplikasi mobile dan lookup item tunggal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'expose data via REST API, serverless' → Amazon API Gateway + Lambda (→ DynamoDB/RDS/Athena)."},{"id":"E1A-31","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"AWS Glue crawler schedules","q":"A data engineer has an AWS Glue crawler that catalogs new partitions in an Amazon S3 data lake. New data lands every 6 hours. The engineer wants the crawler to run every 6 hours with the LEAST operational overhead. What should the engineer do?","o":["Ask an operator to start the crawler manually from the console.","Create an Amazon EC2 instance that runs the AWS CLI start-crawler command from crontab.","Create an Amazon MWAA environment with a DAG that starts the crawler every 6 hours.","Configure a schedule on the crawler by using a cron expression that runs every 6 hours."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: crawler perlu berjalan 'every 6 hours' dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Glue crawler memiliki fitur penjadwalan bawaan berbasis cron expression, sehingga tidak perlu layanan tambahan. Distraktor terdekat adalah MWAA: bisa menjadwalkan crawler, tetapi menyalakan environment Airflow hanya untuk satu jadwal sederhana adalah berlebihan dan mahal. EC2 dengan crontab menambah pengelolaan server, dan menjalankan secara manual tidak bisa diandalkan. Aturan umum: jadwal sederhana untuk crawler atau job Glue = schedule bawaan Glue; orkestrasi kompleks dengan banyak dependensi = MWAA atau Step Functions.","r":["Salah — Proses manual tidak andal dan tidak terotomasi.","Salah — EC2 dengan crontab menambah server yang harus dikelola.","Salah — MWAA berlebihan dan mahal untuk satu jadwal sederhana.","Benar — Jadwal bawaan crawler dengan cron adalah cara paling sederhana tanpa komponen tambahan."],"k":"Jadwal sederhana crawler/job → schedule bawaan Glue (cron)."},{"id":"E2C-20","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Firehose record format conversion and schema changes","q":"An Amazon Data Firehose stream converts incoming JSON records to Apache Parquet by using a table schema in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. The upstream service starts emitting a new field, loyalty_tier, and the field must appear in the Parquet output with minimal changes to the delivery stream. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Add the loyalty_tier column to the Glue table, with the Firehose record format conversion configured to use the LATEST table version.","Disable record format conversion and deliver raw JSON, then convert it later with an Amazon EMR cluster.","Create a new Firehose stream for every new field that the upstream service adds.","Add an AWS Lambda transformation that removes unknown fields from each record."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah field baru harus muncul di output Parquet 'with minimal changes to the delivery stream'. Record format conversion di Amazon Data Firehose memakai schema dari tabel AWS Glue Data Catalog; jika version ID disetel ke LATEST (atau tidak ditentukan), Firehose memakai versi tabel terbaru. Jadi cukup menambahkan kolom loyalty_tier ke tabel Glue dan Firehose akan mulai menulis field tersebut ke Parquet. Mematikan konversi dan menambah cluster EMR menambah komponen dan biaya. Membuat stream baru untuk setiap field tidak skalabel. Lambda yang membuang field justru bertentangan dengan kebutuhan agar field baru muncul. Aturan umum: Firehose JSON→Parquet/ORC mengikuti schema tabel Glue; perbarui tabel dan pakai versi LATEST.","r":["Benar — Firehose membaca schema dari versi tabel Glue terbaru, jadi menambah kolom di tabel cukup untuk menulis field baru.","Salah — Menambah cluster EMR untuk konversi menambah biaya dan overhead padahal Firehose sudah bisa melakukannya.","Salah — Stream baru per field tidak skalabel dan memecah data.","Salah — Membuang field baru bertentangan dengan kebutuhan agar loyalty_tier muncul di output."],"k":"Tips ujian: Firehose konversi ke Parquet + field baru → update tabel Glue (version LATEST)."},{"id":"E3A-55","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Redshift federated query","q":"A company's order data lives in an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database, and historical sales data lives in Amazon Redshift. Analysts need to join live, up-to-the-minute order data with the historical data in one Redshift query. The company does not want to build or maintain an ETL pipeline for this report. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Redshift federated query by creating an external schema that points to the Aurora PostgreSQL database, with credentials stored in AWS Secrets Manager.","Export the Aurora tables to Amazon S3 every night and query them with Redshift Spectrum.","Use AWS DMS to replicate the Aurora tables to Redshift with a nightly full load.","Use Amazon Athena to query Redshift and Aurora and save the result in S3."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'live, up-to-the-minute data', 'join in one Redshift query', dan 'no ETL pipeline'. Redshift federated query memungkinkan Redshift meng-query data operasional langsung di Amazon RDS atau Aurora (PostgreSQL dan MySQL) melalui external schema, dengan kredensial disimpan di Secrets Manager. Query bisa menggabungkan tabel lokal Redshift dan tabel Aurora secara real time tanpa memindahkan data. Ekspor malam ke S3 dan replikasi DMS harian membuat data tertinggal hingga satu hari dan merupakan pipeline yang harus dirawat. Athena federated query bisa menjangkau banyak sumber, tetapi kebutuhannya adalah query di Redshift, dan menyimpan hasil ke S3 menambah langkah. Aturan umum: join data live RDS/Aurora dari Redshift tanpa ETL → Redshift federated query. Untuk replikasi berkelanjutan dalam skala besar, pertimbangkan zero-ETL integration.","r":["Benar — Federated query membaca data Aurora secara live dan menggabungkannya dengan tabel Redshift tanpa ETL.","Salah — Ekspor malam membuat data tertinggal dan merupakan pipeline ETL.","Salah — Full load harian tidak up-to-the-minute dan menambah pipeline yang perlu dirawat.","Salah — Tidak menjawab kebutuhan query di Redshift dan menambah langkah penyimpanan hasil."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Redshift query live data in RDS/Aurora PostgreSQL or MySQL, no ETL' → Redshift federated query."},{"id":"E2A-10","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Redshift RA3 managed storage","q":"A company runs an Amazon Redshift cluster on DC2 nodes. Storage is 90% full and grows 10% each quarter, but CPU utilization rarely exceeds 30%. Adding more DC2 nodes would double compute cost. The company wants to keep query performance and scale storage independently of compute. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Add more DC2 nodes with elastic resize every quarter.","Unload all tables to Amazon S3 and query them only with Amazon Athena.","Migrate the cluster to RA3 nodes that use Redshift Managed Storage.","Enable automatic table compression and run VACUUM DELETE ONLY daily."],"a":[2],"e":"Persyaratan yang menentukan adalah storage hampir penuh sementara CPU rendah, dan keinginan untuk 'scale storage independently of compute' tanpa menurunkan performa. Node RA3 memakai Redshift Managed Storage (RMS) yang menyimpan data di S3 dengan cache SSD lokal, sehingga kapasitas storage tumbuh terpisah dari jumlah node compute. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah node DC2: masalah storage selesai sementara, tetapi membayar compute yang tidak dibutuhkan dan harus diulang tiap kuartal. Kompresi dan VACUUM hanya memberi ruang sedikit dan tidak menyelesaikan pertumbuhan 10% per kuartal. Memindahkan semua ke Athena mengubah arsitektur dan bisa menurunkan performa dashboard. Aturan umum: Redshift dengan storage tumbuh tetapi compute cukup → RA3 dengan managed storage.","r":["Salah — Menambah DC2 menambah compute yang tidak diperlukan, sehingga biaya naik tanpa manfaat CPU.","Salah — Athena atas S3 mengubah pola akses dan tidak menjamin performa query yang sama dengan Redshift.","Benar — RA3 dengan Redshift Managed Storage memisahkan storage dari compute sehingga bisa tumbuh tanpa menambah node.","Salah — Kompresi dan VACUUM hanya menghemat sebagian ruang dan tidak menyelesaikan pertumbuhan data berkelanjutan."],"k":"Redshift storage-bound but compute idle → migrasi ke RA3 (managed storage)."},{"id":"E2C-33","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Athena partition projection","q":"An Athena table is partitioned by year, month, day, and hour and has more than 400,000 partitions. Query planning time has become a large part of total query time, and the team must also run MSCK REPAIR TABLE or a crawler after every new hour of data arrives. The partition values follow a predictable pattern. Which solution reduces query planning time and removes the need for partition maintenance?","o":["Configure partition projection on the table with the date-based ranges and S3 location template.","Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE every 5 minutes instead of every hour.","Merge all partitions into a single partition to reduce the number of partitions.","Increase the Athena workgroup's per-query data usage control limit."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah jumlah partisi sangat besar, waktu query planning tinggi, dan nilai partisi 'follow a predictable pattern'. Partition projection di Athena menghitung nilai partisi dari konfigurasi properti tabel (range tanggal, format, dan template lokasi S3) alih-alih mengambilnya dari Glue Data Catalog, sehingga lookup metadata yang lambat hilang. Partisi baru juga otomatis dikenali tanpa MSCK REPAIR TABLE, ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION, atau crawler. Menjalankan MSCK lebih sering justru menambah beban dan tidak mempercepat planning. Menyatukan semua partisi menghilangkan partition pruning sehingga data yang dipindai melonjak. Batas data usage hanya mengontrol biaya, bukan performa planning. Aturan umum: banyak partisi dengan pola yang dapat diprediksi → Athena partition projection.","r":["Benar — Partition projection menghitung partisi dari konfigurasi sehingga tidak ada lookup katalog dan tidak perlu pemeliharaan partisi.","Salah — MSCK lebih sering menambah beban dan tidak mengurangi waktu planning.","Salah — Tanpa partisi, partition pruning hilang dan data yang dipindai membesar.","Salah — Data usage control membatasi biaya, tidak mempercepat query planning."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena banyak partisi + pola tanggal yang dapat diprediksi → partition projection."},{"id":"E1C-79","d":1,"ts":"1.4.11","t":"Topological sort for job dependencies","q":"A data engineer is writing a small scheduler that must run 30 ETL jobs, where each job declares the jobs it depends on. The scheduler must compute a valid execution order in which every job runs after all of its dependencies, and it must reject configurations in which the dependencies form a cycle. Which algorithm should the engineer use?","o":["Binary search over the sorted list of job names","Topological sort of the directed dependency graph, which fails if a cycle is detected","Sorting the jobs alphabetically by job name","Hashing each job name into a hash table and running jobs in hash order"],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: urutan eksekusi di mana 'every job runs after all of its dependencies' dan menolak konfigurasi yang membentuk 'cycle'. Dependensi job adalah directed graph; topological sort (misalnya algoritma Kahn atau DFS) menghasilkan urutan linear yang menghormati semua edge, dan hanya mungkin jika graf bersifat acyclic (DAG). Jika algoritma tidak dapat memproses semua node, berarti ada siklus dan konfigurasi harus ditolak. Inilah alasan Airflow dan orkestrator lain memodelkan pipeline sebagai DAG. Distractor terdekat adalah urutan hash table: hash table bagus untuk lookup cepat, tetapi urutannya tidak berkaitan dengan dependensi. Binary search dan sort alfabetis juga tidak memperhatikan dependensi. Aturan umum: urutan eksekusi berdasarkan dependensi → topological sort pada DAG; siklus = konfigurasi tidak valid.","r":["Salah — Binary search untuk mencari elemen pada data terurut, bukan untuk menentukan urutan dependensi.","Benar — Topological sort menghasilkan urutan yang valid dan mendeteksi siklus.","Salah — Urutan alfabet tidak berkaitan dengan dependensi.","Salah — Hash table mempercepat lookup tetapi urutannya tidak bermakna."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'order tasks by dependencies' / 'detect circular dependency' → DAG + topological sort."},{"id":"E3A-68","d":3,"ts":"3.2.6","t":"Aggregation with WHERE vs HAVING","q":"An analyst writes an Amazon Athena query to list customers whose total purchases in 2026 exceed 10,000. The query fails: SELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total FROM orders WHERE year = 2026 AND SUM(amount) > 10000 GROUP BY customer_id. How should the query be corrected?","o":["Move SUM(amount) > 10000 into a HAVING clause after GROUP BY customer_id, and keep year = 2026 in the WHERE clause.","Replace SUM(amount) with amount in the WHERE clause.","Move both conditions into the HAVING clause and remove the GROUP BY clause.","Add DISTINCT to the SELECT list."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'total purchases exceed 10,000' (kondisi atas hasil agregasi) dan 'in 2026' (kondisi atas baris). Urutan logis SQL: WHERE memfilter baris sebelum pengelompokan, GROUP BY membentuk grup, lalu HAVING memfilter grup berdasarkan hasil agregasi. Fungsi agregat seperti SUM tidak boleh berada di WHERE karena agregasi belum dihitung pada tahap itu. Jadi year = 2026 tetap di WHERE (sekaligus mengurangi data yang dipindai, terutama jika year adalah kolom partisi), sedangkan SUM(amount) > 10000 dipindah ke HAVING. Mengganti dengan amount > 10000 mengubah arti menjadi transaksi tunggal di atas 10.000, bukan total per customer. Menghapus GROUP BY membuat agregasi per customer hilang. DISTINCT tidak menyelesaikan kesalahan penempatan agregat. Aturan umum: filter baris → WHERE; filter hasil agregasi grup → HAVING.","r":["Benar — HAVING memfilter grup setelah agregasi, sementara WHERE tetap memfilter baris tahun 2026.","Salah — Mengubah makna menjadi transaksi tunggal di atas 10.000, bukan total per customer.","Salah — Tanpa GROUP BY tidak ada total per customer.","Salah — DISTINCT tidak memperbaiki agregat yang salah ditempatkan di WHERE."],"k":"Tips ujian: kondisi atas SUM/COUNT/AVG → HAVING; kondisi atas kolom baris → WHERE."},{"id":"E2B-46","d":2,"ts":"2.3.4","t":"Archiving DynamoDB TTL deletions","q":"An e-commerce company uses DynamoDB TTL to remove shopping cart items 30 days after the last update. For analytics, every item that TTL deletes must be archived to Amazon S3, but items deleted by the application must not be archived. Which TWO steps should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable DynamoDB Streams on the table with a view type that includes the old image.","Configure TTL to write deleted items directly to an S3 bucket.","Process the stream with an AWS Lambda function that keeps only REMOVE records whose userIdentity shows the DynamoDB service principal, and writes them to Amazon S3, for example through Amazon Data Firehose.","Export the table to Amazon S3 once a day by using point-in-time recovery export.","Enable S3 Versioning on the archive bucket to capture TTL deletions."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'every item that TTL deletes must be archived' tetapi 'items deleted by the application must not be archived'. Penghapusan TTL muncul di DynamoDB Streams sebagai event REMOVE; agar isi item tersedia, stream harus memakai view type OLD_IMAGE atau NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES. Record dari TTL punya userIdentity dengan type 'Service' dan principalId 'dynamodb.amazonaws.com', sehingga fungsi Lambda bisa memfilter hanya penghapusan TTL dan menulis datanya ke S3, misalnya lewat Firehose. TTL sendiri tidak punya opsi menulis ke S3. Export harian menyalin seluruh tabel dan tidak bisa membedakan penghapusan TTL dari penghapusan aplikasi. Versioning bucket tidak berkaitan dengan DynamoDB. Ingat: arsip item TTL → Streams (old image) + Lambda filter userIdentity.","r":["Benar — Stream dengan old image membawa isi item yang dihapus sehingga bisa diarsipkan.","Salah — TTL tidak punya fitur menulis item yang dihapus ke S3.","Benar — Filter userIdentity membedakan penghapusan TTL (service principal) dari penghapusan aplikasi.","Salah — Export harian menyalin seluruh tabel dan tidak bisa memisahkan penghapusan TTL.","Salah — Versioning S3 tidak menangkap event penghapusan di DynamoDB."],"k":"Tips ujian: archive TTL-expired items → DynamoDB Streams + Lambda (filter userIdentity principal dynamodb.amazonaws.com) → S3."},{"id":"E2C-09","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"Modeling semi-structured data with Glue Relationalize","q":"A company receives deeply nested JSON order documents (orders contain arrays of line items, and each line item contains an array of discounts). The documents must be loaded into a normalized relational model in Amazon Redshift for BI reporting. The company wants a managed, serverless approach that automatically splits nested arrays into separate child tables with join keys. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use an AWS Glue ETL job with the Relationalize transform to flatten the nested JSON into a root table and child tables, then load them into Redshift.","Use Amazon Athena CTAS statements with UNNEST written manually for every nesting level, and run them from a cron job on Amazon EC2.","Use the Redshift COPY command with the 'auto' JSON option into a single flat table.","Use AWS Glue DataBrew to convert the JSON to CSV and load each CSV into one wide Redshift table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'automatically splits nested arrays into separate child tables with join keys' dan pendekatan managed serverless. Transform Relationalize di AWS Glue mengubah DynamicFrame nested menjadi satu root table dan beberapa child table untuk setiap array, lengkap dengan kolom kunci untuk join, sehingga cocok untuk model relasional di Redshift. Athena dengan UNNEST bisa melakukannya, tetapi harus ditulis manual per level dan dijalankan dari EC2, yang menambah overhead. COPY dengan opsi 'auto' memetakan atribut level atas ke kolom, tetapi tidak memecah array nested menjadi tabel anak. DataBrew ke CSV satu tabel lebar tidak menghasilkan model ternormalisasi dan bisa menggandakan baris. Aturan umum: JSON nested → model relasional ternormalisasi secara otomatis → Glue Relationalize.","r":["Benar — Relationalize memecah struktur nested menjadi root table dan child tables dengan join key secara otomatis dan serverless.","Salah — Query UNNEST manual per level plus EC2 cron menambah pekerjaan dan overhead operasional.","Salah — COPY 'auto' tidak membuat child table dari array nested; hasilnya tabel tunggal yang tidak ternormalisasi.","Salah — Satu tabel CSV lebar bukan model ternormalisasi dan array nested sulit direpresentasikan."],"k":"Tips ujian: nested JSON → tabel relasional parent/child otomatis → AWS Glue Relationalize."},{"id":"E3B-57","d":3,"ts":"3.4.3","t":"Schema consistency with Glue Schema Registry","q":"Multiple producer teams publish Avro events to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. A downstream AWS Glue streaming job keeps failing because producers occasionally change field names or types without notice, which leads to inconsistent records. The company wants to prevent incompatible schema changes from being published while still allowing producers to add optional fields. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler on the stream every hour.","Convert the stream records to JSON so that schemas are not needed.","Use AWS Glue Schema Registry with BACKWARD compatibility mode and have producers and consumers use the registry serializers and deserializers.","Increase the number of shards in the stream."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'prevent incompatible schema changes from being published' sambil 'allowing producers to add optional fields'. AWS Glue Schema Registry menyimpan versi skema Avro/JSON/Protobuf dan menegakkan mode kompatibilitas; dengan BACKWARD compatibility, perubahan seperti menambah field opsional diizinkan, sementara mengganti nama atau tipe field yang memutus kompatibilitas ditolak saat registrasi versi baru. Serializer di sisi producer memvalidasi record terhadap skema terdaftar sebelum dikirim. Distraktor terdekat adalah crawler: hanya mendeteksi skema setelah data masuk, tidak mencegah publikasi. Beralih ke JSON tanpa skema justru menambah inkonsistensi. Menambah shard hanya menaikkan throughput. Aturan: konsistensi skema data streaming → Glue Schema Registry dengan compatibility mode.","r":["Salah — Crawler hanya mendeteksi perubahan setelah data dipublikasikan, tidak mencegahnya.","Salah — Menghapus skema memperburuk konsistensi data.","Benar — Schema Registry menolak versi skema yang tidak kompatibel dan tetap mengizinkan penambahan field opsional.","Salah — Jumlah shard tidak berhubungan dengan konsistensi skema."],"k":"Tips ujian: enforce schema evolution untuk Kinesis/MSK → AWS Glue Schema Registry (compatibility mode)."}]});